00:10:08,567 --> 00:10:10,967
- [Crow] Let's lock 'em
all in relocation camps.

249
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:12,900
- [Joel] Hey, Pink Lady.

250
00:10:12,933 --> 00:10:13,900
- [Admiral King]
These Centaurians

251
00:10:13,933 --> 00:10:15,967
once had a very high culture,
Scott.

252
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:16,800
- [Tom] And Jeff.

253
00:10:16,833 --> 00:10:18,633
- They could again
with our help.

254
00:10:18,667 --> 00:10:20,300
- You sound exactly
like the admiral.

255
00:10:20,333 --> 00:10:22,267
- [Crow] And you sound
like Archie Bunker.

256
00:10:23,367 --> 00:10:25,367
- Your sense of values
have changed.

257
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:26,600
- A deep space colony
can't always live by

258
00:10:26,633 --> 00:10:29,600
the standards we do back home.

259
00:10:29,633 --> 00:10:32,300
- Admiral King's theory
of cosmic colonization.

260
00:10:32,333 --> 00:10:33,433
- [Joel] Is that a Ray
Stevens song?

261
00:10:33,467 --> 00:10:36,633
- It's a required reading
at the academy, Dr. Farrell.

262
00:10:36,667 --> 00:10:40,233
- Commander, if you try
getting to know the admiral,

263
00:10:40,267 --> 00:10:43,167
you might discover he's
quite a remarkable man.

264
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:46,133
- [Joel] And really quite
stunning, when you think about
it.

265
00:10:46,167 --> 00:10:48,833
- I've been with him on
Centaurus
for the past three years.

266
00:10:48,867 --> 00:10:49,667
- [Joel] La dee dah.

267
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:50,800
- I think I know him
pretty well.

268
00:10:50,833 --> 00:10:53,100
- [Joel] And you're no
Jack Kennedy, Senator!

269
00:10:54,533 --> 00:10:56,033
- I believe I know him better.

270
00:10:57,100 --> 00:10:59,500
- [Crow] Yeah, well my
dad can beat up your dad.

271
00:11:02,133 --> 00:11:05,333
- Cosmos Three, Command
Ship One to Cosmos Three.

272
00:11:05,367 --> 00:11:08,400
- [Joel] Disinflating Annette's
hair, starting on my mark.

273
00:11:08,433 --> 00:11:11,000
- If you are receiving,
please acknowledge.

274
00:11:15,567 --> 00:11:16,967
- Shall we keep trying, sir?

275
00:11:19,167 --> 00:11:22,133
- Cosmos Three, this is
Admiral King.

276
00:11:22,167 --> 00:11:25,867
If you are receiving,
please advise Captain Ross

277
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:29,133
that he's off-course and
approaching a dangerous area.

278
00:11:29,167 --> 00:11:31,533
Repeat, your present course

279
00:11:31,567 --> 00:11:33,667
will take you into a
danger zone.

280
00:11:33,700 --> 00:11:34,533
- [Joel] Watts.

281
00:11:35,533 --> 00:11:37,000
- Keep trying.

282
00:11:37,033 --> 00:11:39,200
Repeat the same message,
on all channels.

283
00:11:39,233 --> 00:11:40,533
- [Crow] In your voice, sir?

284
00:11:40,567 --> 00:11:43,867
- Admiral King, do you think
something has happened to them?

285
00:11:43,900 --> 00:11:45,633
- We don't know yet, Linda.

286
00:11:45,667 --> 00:11:48,533
- I have friends aboard
the Cosmos Three.

287
00:11:48,567 --> 00:11:50,633
I am afraid for them.

288
00:11:50,667 --> 00:11:52,567
- We all have friends
on Cosmos Three.

289
00:11:53,867 --> 00:11:55,167
We're all deeply concerned.

290
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:58,067
- [Joel] So concerned that I
felt compelled to touch you.

291
00:12:02,433 --> 00:12:05,933
- Cosmos Fleet Command
Ship One to Cosmos Three.

292
00:12:05,967 --> 00:12:07,800
- [Tom] Pigs in space!

293
00:12:12,967 --> 00:12:14,000
- [Cosmos One] Cosmos One
to Cosmos Three.

294
00:12:14,033 --> 00:12:15,733
- [Joel] They're dead.

295
00:12:15,767 --> 00:12:19,833
- [Cosmos One] If you can
transmit, please acknowledge.

296
00:12:19,867 --> 00:12:22,333
- Tang, you've got to
listen to me. Both of you.

297
00:12:22,367 --> 00:12:24,900
Put away those guns,
it'll soon be too late!

298
00:12:24,933 --> 00:12:25,967
- No.

299
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,800
- [Crow] No way, old man.

300
00:12:27,833 --> 00:12:31,433
- Can't you understand,
this ship is out of control!

301
00:12:31,467 --> 00:12:33,767
Unless you release those
men in the maneuvering room,

302
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:35,900
we're going nowhere but
to our deaths!

303
00:12:35,933 --> 00:12:36,733
- They're trying to trick us.

304
00:12:36,767 --> 00:12:37,933
- I am not trying to--

305
00:12:37,967 --> 00:12:39,133
(punch landing)

306
00:12:39,167 --> 00:12:40,800
- You, Lieutenant Anderson.

307
00:12:40,833 --> 00:12:43,200
You will take us back
to Centaurus.

308
00:12:43,233 --> 00:12:44,500
- You stupid fools!

309
00:12:44,533 --> 00:12:45,933
- [Joel] It's
pronounced Megtaurus.

310
00:12:45,967 --> 00:12:49,033
- He said the Centaurians
couldn't be trusted.

311
00:12:49,067 --> 00:12:50,233
- Tang, what are you doing?

312
00:12:50,267 --> 00:12:52,267
- [Joel] Think of us as
Klingons without the cling.

313
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:53,467
- We're getting back
to Centaurus.

314
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:55,767
- Tang, this is treasonous, do--

315
00:12:59,167 --> 00:13:01,467
- Very strong magnetic field,
sir.

316
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:02,333
We're locked in.

317
00:13:02,367 --> 00:13:04,067
- It's one of the
planets of Solaris.

318
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:06,167
We've entered its
field of gravity.

319
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,567
- Activate the decelerator,
sergeant.

320
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,633
- What does it mean, captain?

321
00:13:08,667 --> 00:13:09,733
- It's no use.

322
00:13:10,867 --> 00:13:13,767
It means that we're doomed
to crash into that planet

323
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:16,433
unless I can regain control
of the maneuvering room.

324
00:13:16,467 --> 00:13:18,100
- [All] Not again!

325
00:13:18,133 --> 00:13:20,200
- [Tom] And that playground
ball's a threat too.

326
00:13:20,233 --> 00:13:21,567
- Then we shall crash.

327
00:13:22,567 --> 00:13:25,533
It is better that we
die than be your slaves.

328
00:13:25,567 --> 00:13:27,267
- We have never treated
you as a slave.

329
00:13:27,300 --> 00:13:28,933
- [Crow] Yeah, what about
that one time?

330
00:13:28,967 --> 00:13:30,200
- The captain knows
what it's about--

331
00:13:30,233 --> 00:13:33,067
(punches landing)

332
00:13:38,467 --> 00:13:41,033
- [Tom] We're gonna crash
into a Universal picture!

333
00:13:42,100 --> 00:13:45,667
(instrumental theme music)

334
00:13:48,933 --> 00:13:51,200
(whirring)

335
00:13:55,133 --> 00:13:56,467
- [Joel] Fakey.

336
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:01,933
- [All] Fakey.

337
00:14:03,033 --> 00:14:03,867
Real.

338
00:14:05,833 --> 00:14:06,733
- [Joel] Dead guy.

339
00:14:06,767 --> 00:14:08,533
- [All] Fakey.

340
00:14:08,567 --> 00:14:09,400
Real.

341
00:14:10,967 --> 00:14:12,500
- [Tom] Real fakey.

342
00:14:12,533 --> 00:14:13,233
- [Joel] Fake guys.

343
00:14:14,333 --> 00:14:17,100
Filmed on location in
Tommy Ronick's front yard.

344
00:14:17,133 --> 00:14:19,467
(splashing)

345
00:14:20,433 --> 00:14:23,167
(dramatic music)

346
00:14:28,467 --> 00:14:30,000
- [Tom] They're hammered.

347
00:14:30,033 --> 00:14:31,300
- [Joel] And the
chicks are dead.

348
00:14:36,633 --> 00:14:38,133
- What do you suppose
happened to them, admiral?

349
00:14:38,167 --> 00:14:40,700
- [Crow] Ah, they probably
crashed in Tommy's front yard.

350
00:14:41,833 --> 00:14:42,933
- Cosmic clouds.

351
00:14:42,967 --> 00:14:46,233
- [Joel] Yellow moons, pink
hearts, all that stuff.

352
00:14:46,267 --> 00:14:47,100
- It shouldn't.

353
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:49,733
- I wonder how they got so
far off-course.

354
00:14:49,767 --> 00:14:51,800
I mean, it's impossible
they didn't know.

355
00:14:52,833 --> 00:14:54,567
- No question about it, admiral.

356
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:57,367
They're grounded on one of
the inner planets of Solaris.

357
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:58,233
- [Joel] Yikes.

358
00:14:58,267 --> 00:14:59,533
- Communications,
anything coming in?

359
00:14:59,567 --> 00:15:01,700
- No, admiral, nothing
but the homing signal.

360
00:15:01,733 --> 00:15:04,400
- Any reply from
command headquarters?

361
00:15:04,433 --> 00:15:05,933
- Nothing yet, admiral.

362
00:15:05,967 --> 00:15:07,033
- Keep me informed.

363
00:15:07,067 --> 00:15:07,900
- [Crow] Well, that's not
gonna be easy.

364
00:15:07,933 --> 00:15:09,533
You're kind of a muttonhead.

365
00:15:09,567 --> 00:15:11,733
(beeping)

366
00:15:14,067 --> 00:15:15,867
- The admiral is really upset,
isn't he?

367
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:16,767
- [Joel] Hmm, yeah.

368
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:18,433
- It's the first ship
he's ever lost.

369
00:15:18,467 --> 00:15:21,133
- [Tom] Lost his keys a few
times, but never the whole ship.

370
00:15:21,167 --> 00:15:23,133
- Do you think he
will turn back?

371
00:15:23,167 --> 00:15:24,167
- [Joel] Probably.

372
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:25,833
- If command'll let him,
he will.

373
00:15:27,267 --> 00:15:30,600
- I don't think so,
we're too close to home.

374
00:15:30,633 --> 00:15:32,300
- You know we'll
never get there.

375
00:15:33,367 --> 00:15:34,967
It is just a wishful dream.

376
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,500
- I know what you mean, honey.

377
00:15:36,533 --> 00:15:38,100
- [Crow] Uh-oh.

378
00:15:38,133 --> 00:15:39,800
Moron patrol.

379
00:15:39,833 --> 00:15:43,567
- This isn't exactly what
I call a pleasure party.

380
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:46,067
- Well it could be, sugar,
if you'd let yourself go.

381
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:48,900
- Well, well, the wolf
of outer space.

382
00:15:48,933 --> 00:15:51,533
And who let you out of
your darkened den?

383
00:15:51,567 --> 00:15:52,867
- Now be kind to me, ladies.

384
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:55,267
Don't forget that I'm
your ingenious engineer,

385
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:56,900
the master of the
maneuvering room

386
00:15:56,933 --> 00:15:59,133
and the activator of
your gravity.

387
00:15:59,167 --> 00:16:01,833
- [Tom] Not to mention
a flatulating butthead.

388
00:16:02,833 --> 00:16:04,033
- Here we go again.

389
00:16:04,067 --> 00:16:06,067
Well I suppose we are grateful

390
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:09,133
for all these amazing
services, Mr. Bradley.

391
00:16:09,167 --> 00:16:11,633
- Lieutenant, you just
allow this sweet thing

392
00:16:11,667 --> 00:16:13,533
a few moments' liberty
with your little star mate

393
00:16:13,567 --> 00:16:17,100
and well, I'll consider
you all paid in full.

394
00:16:18,500 --> 00:16:21,467
- [Joel] He's done everything
but insult the Centaurian.

395
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:22,767
- Now Lieutenant,
there's no reason

396
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:25,267
for you to treat me like
a common old Centaurian.

397
00:16:27,933 --> 00:16:28,733
- [All] Oops.

398
00:16:28,767 --> 00:16:30,300
- Hey Linda, I'm sorry.

399
00:16:30,333 --> 00:16:32,700
You know I didn't mean
anything by what I said.

400
00:16:36,867 --> 00:16:39,333
You know me, I could
light up a whole room.

401
00:16:39,367 --> 00:16:40,900
(laughing)

402
00:16:40,933 --> 00:16:42,600
Just by walking out.

403
00:16:42,633 --> 00:16:44,667
- [All] Yay.
(clapping)

404
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:49,833
- Forget it, Linda, he
didn't mean it.

405
00:16:49,867 --> 00:16:51,167
- You know, she's right.

406
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:53,633
I mean, Lieutenant
Bradley's crazy about you.

407
00:16:53,667 --> 00:16:56,433
- [Crow] Hey, check out
those space-age lockers.

408
00:16:56,467 --> 00:16:58,533
- You know that.

409
00:16:58,567 --> 00:16:59,467
- Yes, I know.

410
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:03,767
But I wonder if your people
really can accept us, Karen.

411
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:07,733
- Listen Linda, you
have an exciting

412
00:17:07,767 --> 00:17:08,933
new life ahead of you.

413
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,600
Don't worry about
being accepted.

414
00:17:11,633 --> 00:17:13,367
- [Tom] 'Cause you won't be.

415
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:14,767
- When you get around to
all those young cadets

416
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:17,333
at the academy, you'll
forget all about Centaurus,

417
00:17:17,367 --> 00:17:21,867
those years in the colonies
and people with narrow minds.

418
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:23,533
- [Crow] Among other things.

419
00:17:23,567 --> 00:17:25,333
- You know, I've
barely ever seen

420
00:17:25,367 --> 00:17:26,167
a boy of my own age.

421
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:27,333
- [Joel] I'm
resetting the controls

422
00:17:27,367 --> 00:17:29,800
so they crash into the
prehistoric planet.

423
00:17:29,833 --> 00:17:31,767
- Command headquarters!

424
00:17:42,300 --> 00:17:43,767
(beeping)

425
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:45,400
- [Crow] Do I look good up here?

426
00:17:46,767 --> 00:17:48,833
- The reply from Space Command,
Mr. Scott.

427
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,833
- [Joel] It says, "Do not
tear, spindle or mutilate!"

428
00:17:55,067 --> 00:17:56,867
- Communique from headquarters,
admiral.

429
00:17:58,333 --> 00:17:59,133
- [Joel] Looks like your agent's

430
00:17:59,167 --> 00:18:00,500
not gonna get you
outta this one.

431
00:18:00,533 --> 00:18:03,033
- No other communications
can be established,

432
00:18:03,067 --> 00:18:05,433
it must be assumed that
Cosmos Three has crashed,

433
00:18:05,467 --> 00:18:07,533
killing all crew members
and passengers.

434
00:18:07,567 --> 00:18:08,767
- [Joel] He's right.

435
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:10,900
- We regret your request to
return to star system Solaris

436
00:18:10,933 --> 00:18:13,933
to search for survivors
must be denied.

437
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:16,667
Continue on course
as programmed.

438
00:18:16,700 --> 00:18:18,367
- [Joel] Signed,
Zippy the chimp.

439
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:19,667
- [Tom] Huh?

440
00:18:19,700 --> 00:18:22,333
- It would have been a
futile effort, admiral.

441
00:18:22,367 --> 00:18:24,567
- We will reverse our course,
Mr. Scott.

442
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:28,600
Program a flight plan
to take us to Solaris.

443
00:18:28,633 --> 00:18:29,667
- But sir, the request has been

444
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:31,233
denied by Command headquarters.

445
00:18:31,267 --> 00:18:33,300
- I'm the commander
of this fleet.

446
00:18:33,333 --> 00:18:35,400
All the passengers and
crewmen on these ships

447
00:18:35,433 --> 00:18:38,833
are my responsibility as
long as we are in deep space.

448
00:18:38,867 --> 00:18:40,767
We are still in space.

449
00:18:41,733 --> 00:18:43,300
- [Crow] Well, they're in
deep something.

450
00:18:44,767 --> 00:18:46,067
- Is that clear, Mr. Scott?

451
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:47,600
- [Joel] Hold me.
- Yes, sir.

452
00:18:49,667 --> 00:18:51,733
- Send a communique to
Command headquarters

453
00:18:51,767 --> 00:18:53,200
to that effect immediately.

454
00:18:57,167 --> 00:18:59,133
- Evans, stand by to
reverse course.

455
00:18:59,167 --> 00:19:00,500
Horizontal maneuver.
- Yes, sir.

456
00:19:00,533 --> 00:19:01,567
- [Joel] That's how he
got that job.

457
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:02,933
- Maneuvering room,
this is Control.

458
00:19:02,967 --> 00:19:05,900
Stand by horixontal activators,
we're changing course.

459
00:19:05,933 --> 00:19:06,933
- [Crow] And beam up more Dep.

460
00:19:06,967 --> 00:19:09,033
- Maneuvering room standing by.

461
00:19:09,067 --> 00:19:11,100
- I'll talk to you later, sugar.

462
00:19:11,133 --> 00:19:14,400
- [Joel] I just made out on
the phone, this is great!

463
00:19:14,433 --> 00:19:15,967
- What is all this, Mr. Bradley?

464
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,533
First we slow down to a walk.

465
00:19:17,567 --> 00:19:19,567
- [Joel] It's a control
panel, you should know that.

466
00:19:19,600 --> 00:19:21,800
- Looks like we're going back,
chief.

467
00:19:21,833 --> 00:19:24,500
- You mean Space Command
okayed the old man's request?

468
00:19:24,533 --> 00:19:25,533
- Well if they didn't,

469
00:19:25,567 --> 00:19:27,467
he's sure gonna catch
it when we do get home.

470
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,233
- Maneuvering room from Control.

471
00:19:29,267 --> 00:19:33,733
New course is one-seven-five
degrees on horizontal plane.

472
00:19:33,767 --> 00:19:36,633
- One-seven-five horizontal.

473
00:19:36,667 --> 00:19:39,933
(switches clicking)

474
00:19:39,967 --> 00:19:40,767
- Programmed.

475
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:41,867
- [Tom] That's all
you have to do?

476
00:19:41,900 --> 00:19:44,100
- Set automatic pilot on
Cosmos Three's homing beam

477
00:19:44,133 --> 00:19:46,800
for three months' cruising,
full acceleration.

478
00:19:46,833 --> 00:19:47,933
- Three months?

479
00:19:47,967 --> 00:19:48,800
Yes, sir.

480
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:53,033
- [Joel] I got this Snoopy
ruler for free.

481
00:19:53,067 --> 00:19:54,733
What do you think, Tom?

482
00:19:54,767 --> 00:19:55,600
Anybody?

483
00:20:04,033 --> 00:20:06,400
- [Tom] People always seem
to comfort her.

484
00:20:06,433 --> 00:20:09,167
(dramatic music)

485
00:20:11,133 --> 00:20:13,333
- [Crow] Even our name
says Merry Christmas.

486
00:20:20,933 --> 00:20:21,733
- [Crow] Gilligan!

487
00:20:21,767 --> 00:20:23,067
- [Tom] Skipper!

488
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:24,367
- [Crow] Gilligan!

489
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:25,733
- [Tom] Skipper!

490
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:28,233
- [Crow] Mary Anne!

491
00:20:28,267 --> 00:20:29,900
- [Tom] Ginger!

492
00:20:29,933 --> 00:20:30,767
Thurston?

493
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:31,600
- [Crow] Lovey?

494
00:20:31,633 --> 00:20:32,600
- [Tom] Wrong-way?

495
00:20:32,633 --> 00:20:33,800
- [Crow] Japanese guy!

496
00:20:42,267 --> 00:20:43,867
Hey, the mummy's getting better.

497
00:20:49,633 --> 00:20:51,767
- We'll stop here for the night.

498
00:20:51,800 --> 00:20:53,467
At least it's dry ground.

499
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:57,000
- [Crow] Yeah, rest here,
maybe we can find your scalp.

500
00:20:57,033 --> 00:20:58,467
Hey, here's some mossy lichen.

501
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:00,333
We could make a wig out
of it for ya.

502
00:21:00,367 --> 00:21:01,800
- Don't touch me!

503
00:21:01,833 --> 00:21:03,467
I told you to stay away from me.

504
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:05,000
- I only want to help you,
lieutenant.

505
00:21:05,033 --> 00:21:06,000
You need help.

506
00:21:06,033 --> 00:21:07,267
- [Joel] Yeah, but you
put my arm in a sling

507
00:21:07,300 --> 00:21:08,100
and it doesn't even hurt.

508
00:21:08,133 --> 00:21:09,467
- None of us would
need any help.

509
00:21:10,633 --> 00:21:13,900
- I'm sorry for what has
happened, but I didn't rebel.

510
00:21:13,933 --> 00:21:16,133
- Jang was your brother,
what's the difference?

511
00:21:16,167 --> 00:21:17,633
- Jang thinks for himself.

512
00:21:17,667 --> 00:21:18,900
I am not responsible.

513
00:21:19,767 --> 00:21:20,833
- You're all alike.

514
00:21:20,867 --> 00:21:24,033
You take everything from
us and you give nothing.

515
00:21:24,067 --> 00:21:25,700
I hate all of you.

516
00:21:25,733 --> 00:21:26,967
- But Sally, we were friends
only a few hours ago,

517
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:28,633
- [Tom] I'm Johnny Longtorso.

518
00:21:28,667 --> 00:21:30,700
Can I be of any help here?

519
00:21:30,733 --> 00:21:32,633
- Leave me alone, please!

520
00:21:37,833 --> 00:21:39,333
- [Crow] Maybe this
isn't a good time,

521
00:21:39,367 --> 00:21:41,667
but could you launder my pants?

522
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:43,400
- No, Zenda, I don't
hate you but...

523
00:21:44,433 --> 00:21:47,000
- But you wish you'd
never heard of Centaurus.

524
00:21:47,033 --> 00:21:48,900
- I didn't say that.

525
00:21:48,933 --> 00:21:50,967
- [Joel] Let's just say
that I don't hate you.

526
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:52,600
I'm not gonna call you
for racquetball,

527
00:21:52,633 --> 00:21:53,833
if that's what you mean.

528
00:22:00,700 --> 00:22:02,200
I wonder what she wanted.

529
00:22:03,733 --> 00:22:06,133
- [Tom] Here's my card,
Johnny Longtorso.

530
00:22:08,133 --> 00:22:09,667
- Here, Sally.

531
00:22:09,700 --> 00:22:10,600
- [Joel] It's Pez.

532
00:22:10,633 --> 00:22:11,700
Make you feel better.

533
00:22:13,467 --> 00:22:14,567
- It'll kill the pain.

534
00:22:17,133 --> 00:22:19,933
- [Crow] And here, it's
my Motorman's Helper.

535
00:22:19,967 --> 00:22:20,933
- [Joel] Finish it!

536
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:24,567
- I wish I could do more.

537
00:22:25,700 --> 00:22:27,033
I wish I were a doctor.

538
00:22:27,067 --> 00:22:30,100
- [Joel] I wish I were a
pixie, but let's get real.

539
00:22:30,967 --> 00:22:32,800
- You wished for her
and you got her.

540
00:22:34,267 --> 00:22:36,700
What did I get, nothing.

541
00:22:36,733 --> 00:22:38,967
Well I'm gonna try wishing.

542
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:40,233
I wish I was dead!

543
00:22:41,300 --> 00:22:42,533
- [Tom] That can be arranged.

544
00:22:42,567 --> 00:22:44,133
- We're gonna be all right.

545
00:22:44,167 --> 00:22:46,333
Admiral King'll come
back for us.

546
00:22:46,367 --> 00:22:48,867
Cosmos One's probably on its
way here this very minute.

547
00:22:48,900 --> 00:22:51,100
- [Tom] And hey, you got
a sling outta the deal

548
00:22:51,133 --> 00:22:51,933
and it's a pretty neat one.

549
00:22:51,967 --> 00:22:53,400
- Even if they know
where we are.

550
00:22:54,633 --> 00:22:57,300
Command headquarters will
never let him turn back.

551
00:22:57,333 --> 00:22:58,800
- [Joel] We're too
annoying for anyone

552
00:22:58,833 --> 00:23:01,133
to consider picking us up,
it's over.

553
00:23:01,167 --> 00:23:02,700
- I know Admiral King too,

554
00:23:04,133 --> 00:23:06,100
Anyway, we've got to hope,
Sally.

555
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:12,133
- [Crow] Nice speech,
now can I get some sleep,

556
00:23:12,167 --> 00:23:13,233
for goodness sake?

557
00:23:15,500 --> 00:23:16,233
- [Joel] Nice statue.

558
00:23:16,267 --> 00:23:17,333
Oh, she's real.

559
00:23:17,367 --> 00:23:20,167
- [Tom] Weren't you in
Bali H'ai, or Hawaiian Eye?

560
00:23:22,233 --> 00:23:24,700
- You'd better get some rest,
Zenda.

561
00:23:24,733 --> 00:23:25,700
We may have a long way to go

562
00:23:25,733 --> 00:23:27,233
before we get out of
this jungle.

563
00:23:28,467 --> 00:23:31,167
- Do you really believe
they'll be back to look for us?

564
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:32,167
- Of course I do.

565
00:23:34,467 --> 00:23:35,333
- You're a good man, Charles.

566
00:23:35,367 --> 00:23:36,267
- [Crow] Brown.

567
00:23:36,300 --> 00:23:39,167
- Your faith and courage,
even in defeat.

568
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:40,233
- [Tom] And my feet look
like hell right now.

569
00:23:40,267 --> 00:23:41,333
- We're still alive.

570
00:23:44,367 --> 00:23:47,267
Tomorrow we should be able
to reach the foothills.

571
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:48,333
It's safer there.

572
00:23:48,367 --> 00:23:51,233
- [Joel] If I read my
script correctly, that is.

573
00:23:51,267 --> 00:23:53,033
- We can still live
on this planet,

574
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:56,400
if we just trust each other.

575
00:23:58,567 --> 00:24:01,333
- [Tom] We can play
boobly-oobly for years,

576
00:24:01,367 --> 00:24:03,167
and the banana will stick.

577
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:05,067
- [Joel] Oh, we better
get out of here.

578
00:24:05,100 --> 00:24:07,500
- [Crow] Wonder what she wanted.

579
00:24:07,533 --> 00:24:12,533
(mechanical whirring)
(doors closing)

580
00:24:17,633 --> 00:24:20,933
- Joel, this is your life!

581
00:24:20,967 --> 00:24:23,833
(applauding)

582
00:24:23,867 --> 00:24:26,367
you were an ambitious young man
and began your life in space

583
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:29,000
as a custodian for
Gizmonic Institute.

584
00:24:29,033 --> 00:24:30,900
Do you remember this voice?

585
00:24:30,933 --> 00:24:32,533
- [Crow] There's an
unidentified satellite

586
00:24:32,567 --> 00:24:34,333
straying into our orbital path!

587
00:24:34,367 --> 00:24:37,100
- Oh, well that's easy,
it's my old friend Crow.

588
00:24:37,133 --> 00:24:39,000
I think he's talking
about the time we partied

589
00:24:39,033 --> 00:24:40,967
with the fellas from
Salyut Seven.

590
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:42,000
(grunting)

591
00:24:42,033 --> 00:24:43,267
- Joel, Joel, help!

592
00:24:43,300 --> 00:24:45,133
Big satellite, big, death,

593
00:24:45,167 --> 00:24:46,600
danger, wreckage, ouch!

594
00:24:46,633 --> 00:24:48,100
Thing, pain.

595
00:24:48,133 --> 00:24:50,167
Hey, where did this
couch come from anyway?

596
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:52,867
- I found it in one of the
crates down in the loading bay.

597
00:24:52,900 --> 00:24:54,000
I thought I'd redecorate.

598
00:24:54,033 --> 00:24:55,867
What's this about a
death satellite?

599
00:24:55,900 --> 00:24:56,700
- Oh yeah.

600
00:24:56,733 --> 00:24:58,133
A big, big death satellite.

601
00:24:58,167 --> 00:24:58,967
Oh, big.

602
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:00,400
Pain, look, run.

603
00:25:00,433 --> 00:25:01,233
Help, help.

604
00:25:01,267 --> 00:25:02,333
- Just settle down,
come up here.

605
00:25:02,367 --> 00:25:04,133
Come on up here and sit down.

606
00:25:04,167 --> 00:25:06,733
Tell me all about it, okay,
just take a few deep breaths.

607
00:25:06,767 --> 00:25:07,500
That's all right.

608
00:25:07,533 --> 00:25:08,467
(breathing deeply)

609
00:25:08,500 --> 00:25:11,200
- Well, there's a big
satellite out there

610
00:25:11,233 --> 00:25:13,000
and we're gonna collide with it.

611
00:25:13,033 --> 00:25:13,767
- What!?

612
00:25:13,800 --> 00:25:14,833
- Ow!
(clattering)

613
00:25:14,867 --> 00:25:17,867
- Cambot, give me an
exterior of the ship, quick!

614
00:25:17,900 --> 00:25:18,933
Jeepers!

615
00:25:18,967 --> 00:25:20,800
- [Crow] What's goin' on?

616
00:25:20,833 --> 00:25:22,033
- Get behind the couch, you two.

617
00:25:22,067 --> 00:25:24,000
The redcoats are coming.

618
00:25:24,033 --> 00:25:25,800
All right, little
death satellite.

619
00:25:25,833 --> 00:25:28,367
Joely's got the exo-pincers on

620
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:30,733
and he's nobody's sweetheart.

621
00:25:30,767 --> 00:25:34,700
You and me, going round
and round, mano y mano.

622
00:25:34,733 --> 00:25:36,267
Here comes lunch.

623
00:25:36,300 --> 00:25:37,333
Gimme the exo.

624
00:25:38,300 --> 00:25:40,167
That's right, little
doomsday machine.

625
00:25:40,200 --> 00:25:43,600
Come to papa, feel my steel.

626
00:25:43,633 --> 00:25:44,867
Hah hah hah.

627
00:25:44,900 --> 00:25:46,533
Now to bring it inside.

628
00:25:46,567 --> 00:25:48,533
Cambot, gimme the interior shot.

629
00:25:49,667 --> 00:25:51,467
- Do you have to bring
everything you find in space

630
00:25:51,500 --> 00:25:52,633
into the living room?

631
00:25:52,667 --> 00:25:54,833
- Sure looks like a
doomsday device, all right.

632
00:25:54,867 --> 00:25:56,700
Joel, are we up a creek here?

633
00:25:56,733 --> 00:25:59,033
- It's a doomsday machine,
all right, and I think

634
00:25:59,067 --> 00:26:02,567
I accidentally activated
its self-destruct mechanism.

635
00:26:02,600 --> 00:26:05,867
I'd say we have roughly an
hour to disarm this thing.

636
00:26:05,900 --> 00:26:08,900
- [Satellite] Correction, you
have an hour and 37 minutes

637
00:26:08,933 --> 00:26:11,233
to disarm and yes, you
are up a creek.

638
00:26:11,267 --> 00:26:13,100
- Oh, golly.

639
00:26:13,133 --> 00:26:15,533
And we got commercial
sign on top of everything!

640
00:26:16,533 --> 00:26:20,133
(instrumental theme music)

641
00:26:26,733 --> 00:26:28,667
We gotta disarm that satellite,
you two,

642
00:26:28,700 --> 00:26:30,933
or this is serious.

643
00:26:30,967 --> 00:26:32,633
- [Tom] Going down
for the count.

644
00:26:35,100 --> 00:26:37,000
- [Crow] That was no
boating accident!

645
00:26:38,567 --> 00:26:40,067
- [Tom] I'm sorry I had to
kill you, Dave,

646
00:26:40,100 --> 00:26:41,767
but you understand, I
couldn't let you live.

647
00:26:41,800 --> 00:26:43,600
You see, you knew too much.

648
00:26:47,267 --> 00:26:49,500
- [Joel] It's the Green Hornet.

649
00:26:49,533 --> 00:26:50,367
- [Crow] Kato?

650
00:26:55,733 --> 00:26:58,467
(Joel whistling)

651
00:27:13,533 --> 00:27:14,500
- [Crow] You'd think
in the future

652
00:27:14,533 --> 00:27:16,333
they'd be able to
get hip waders.

653
00:27:20,067 --> 00:27:21,267
- [Tom] Oh, very sneaky.

654
00:27:24,367 --> 00:27:27,233
- [Joel] Hey, he's trying to
sneak across the rice paper.

655
00:27:37,133 --> 00:27:40,000
- [Crow] If only I could
get to my utility belt.

656
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:44,900
(Crow growls)

657
00:27:46,467 --> 00:27:47,267
- [Tom] Smooth.

658
00:27:47,300 --> 00:27:48,433
- [Crow] I'll take that, Mr.
Bond.

659
00:27:48,467 --> 00:27:49,367
- What are you trying to do?

660
00:27:49,400 --> 00:27:50,500
- Someone's out there.

661
00:27:51,900 --> 00:27:52,933
- [Joel] Who could
be out there--

662
00:27:52,967 --> 00:27:53,800
Huh?

663
00:27:56,633 --> 00:27:58,533
- [Tom] Take that, Mr. Moto!

664
00:27:58,567 --> 00:28:00,567
Nerts to you, Confucius.

665
00:28:12,033 --> 00:28:15,200
- [Joel] Bring the car around...

666
00:28:16,400 --> 00:28:17,633
Kato.

667
00:28:17,667 --> 00:28:20,000
- You will not take us back!

668
00:28:22,500 --> 00:28:26,167
- [Crow] Strange way for lodge
brothers to greet each other.

669
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:28,467
- [Tom] Don't just do
something, stand there!

670
00:28:32,800 --> 00:28:35,933
- [Crow] Tiny bubbles
in my larynx!

671
00:28:36,833 --> 00:28:40,067
(Tom imitates choking)

672
00:28:43,267 --> 00:28:46,367
- [Joel] I'm not on either side,
oop.

673
00:28:52,933 --> 00:28:54,333
- [Tom] Kill your
brother, it's the only way

674
00:28:54,367 --> 00:28:57,000
to reinforce the director's
white male reality.

675
00:29:00,467 --> 00:29:02,067
Take the shot, come on!

676
00:29:08,033 --> 00:29:10,467
(gun firing)

677
00:29:12,633 --> 00:29:15,867
- [Joel] Mom always did
like you best.

678
00:29:19,267 --> 00:29:20,833
- [Crow] Gee, I...

679
00:29:20,867 --> 00:29:21,700
I missed.

680
00:29:29,067 --> 00:29:30,733
- [Joel] I know you
just shot your brother,

681
00:29:30,767 --> 00:29:33,333
but why don't you just
come over here

682
00:29:33,367 --> 00:29:35,900
and love me a little bit?

683
00:29:35,933 --> 00:29:36,767
Yeah.

684
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:43,100
Hey, help me.

685
00:29:47,667 --> 00:29:49,367
- [Tom] Meanwhile, at
the ocarina.

686
00:29:52,300 --> 00:29:53,633
- 10,000 miles, sir.

687
00:29:53,667 --> 00:29:56,000
- Plot speed miles, five
miles per second.

688
00:29:56,033 --> 00:29:58,000
Alright, Alan, check
gravitation compensators

689
00:29:58,033 --> 00:29:59,733
for an altitude of 50 miles.

690
00:29:59,767 --> 00:30:01,267
Decelerate to zero velocity.

691
00:30:01,300 --> 00:30:04,167
- DC 50 miles, zero velocity.

692
00:30:09,867 --> 00:30:10,667
500.

693
00:30:10,700 --> 00:30:12,200
- [Joel] 500 what?

694
00:30:15,067 --> 00:30:15,867
- 300.

695
00:30:15,900 --> 00:30:17,433
- [Joel] What?

696
00:30:17,467 --> 00:30:18,267
- 200.

697
00:30:18,300 --> 00:30:19,333
- [Joel] Stop teasing me.

698
00:30:19,367 --> 00:30:20,467
- [Alan] 150.

699
00:30:22,067 --> 00:30:22,867
100.

700
00:30:22,900 --> 00:30:23,767
- [Crow] Sold.

701
00:30:23,800 --> 00:30:24,833
- 75.

702
00:30:24,867 --> 00:30:25,700
60, 55.

703
00:30:27,833 --> 00:30:28,633
50.

704
00:30:28,667 --> 00:30:29,867
- [Crow] And so on and so on.

705
00:30:29,900 --> 00:30:32,033
- Stationary orbit, sir.

706
00:30:32,067 --> 00:30:33,767
- 50 miles and locked in, sir.

707
00:30:33,800 --> 00:30:34,933
- Very good, Mr. Scott.

708
00:30:34,967 --> 00:30:36,467
- [Tom] Told you he'd like it.

709
00:30:38,267 --> 00:30:40,000
- [Joel] Hey, Picture Picture.

710
00:30:40,033 --> 00:30:42,067
- Could you join me on the
observation deck, please?

711
00:30:43,267 --> 00:30:44,967
- [Crow] He asked me,
he asked me!

712
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:48,500
- [Joel] Just let me
slip my dance belt on.

713
00:30:48,533 --> 00:30:49,533
- We've finally arrived.

714
00:30:49,567 --> 00:30:52,367
- Did you have any doubts,
doctor?

715
00:30:52,400 --> 00:30:53,900
- About reaching Solaris?

716
00:30:53,933 --> 00:30:54,933
No.

717
00:30:54,967 --> 00:30:56,800
- [Tom] Let's see, looks
like a hairline fracture.

718
00:30:56,833 --> 00:30:58,833
- What about finding any of
them still alive, Dr. Farrell?

719
00:30:59,967 --> 00:31:01,200
- Well, there's always a chance.

720
00:31:01,233 --> 00:31:03,500
- Not a very good chance,
I believe.

721
00:31:03,533 --> 00:31:05,433
- [Crow] Oh what do you know?

722
00:31:05,467 --> 00:31:08,100
- Yes, the facts do
indicate that this planet

723
00:31:08,133 --> 00:31:11,833
has an unpleasant environment,
but not necessarily hostile.

724
00:31:11,867 --> 00:31:14,667
It has a carbon water
oxygen system.

725
00:31:14,700 --> 00:31:16,600
- [Joel] Sounds kinda
like a Slurpee.

726
00:31:16,633 --> 00:31:18,800
(speaking foreign language)

727
00:31:18,833 --> 00:31:20,067
- [Crow] Hmm?

728
00:31:20,100 --> 00:31:22,833
- Jung has calculated
that for the past

729
00:31:22,867 --> 00:31:24,767
three months while we've
been traveling,

730
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:27,067
18 years have gone by
on the planet.

731
00:31:28,667 --> 00:31:31,267
- [Tom] That means it'll be
legal to date my girlfriend now.

732
00:31:31,300 --> 00:31:34,400
- [Joel] My CDs should be
rolling over just about now.

733
00:31:34,433 --> 00:31:36,733
- I believe our admiral
will not give up

734
00:31:36,767 --> 00:31:39,633
until he has definite proof
there are no survivors.

735
00:31:39,667 --> 00:31:41,067
- [Crow] He's gonna get
sleeves someday.

736
00:31:41,100 --> 00:31:43,000
- It'll probably cost
him his command.

737
00:31:44,933 --> 00:31:48,233
- Once there were such
leaders on Centaurus.

738
00:31:48,267 --> 00:31:51,300
- If the admiral has his
way, there will be again.

739
00:31:51,333 --> 00:31:52,467
He's determined to prove that

740
00:31:52,500 --> 00:31:54,367
Centaurus can rebuild
its culture.

741
00:31:54,400 --> 00:31:55,600
- [Joel] What a kiss-up.

742
00:31:58,967 --> 00:32:00,567
- Well, I'd say that Linda is

743
00:32:00,600 --> 00:32:02,700
a brilliant example of
what can be done.

744
00:32:02,733 --> 00:32:04,500
- [Crow] Through bizarre
experimentation.

745
00:32:04,533 --> 00:32:08,800
- When she was removed to the
colony, the others were not.

746
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:12,033
- What are you trying to
tell me, Jung?

747
00:32:12,067 --> 00:32:15,300
- [Tom] I abhor you,
round-eye, and all your ways.

748
00:32:15,333 --> 00:32:17,733
- A people will
change their ways

749
00:32:17,767 --> 00:32:20,233
only if they wish to do so.

750
00:32:21,633 --> 00:32:24,067
A man may be removed
from the land.

751
00:32:24,100 --> 00:32:25,667
- [Crow] Wait, wait, let
me get a pencil here.

752
00:32:25,700 --> 00:32:29,400
- But it is difficult to
remove the land from the man.

753
00:32:29,433 --> 00:32:32,333
- [All] And you can't remove
the land from the man,

754
00:32:32,367 --> 00:32:35,300
the chalice from the palace
has the brew that is true.

755
00:32:36,767 --> 00:32:37,567
- [Tom] The flagon
with the dragon

756
00:32:37,600 --> 00:32:38,933
has the pellet with the poison.

757
00:32:41,200 --> 00:32:43,400
- It's such a beautiful planet.

758
00:32:43,433 --> 00:32:45,833
- [Joel] Hey, settle down,
it's just a painting.

759
00:32:47,967 --> 00:32:49,167
- So clean and peaceful.

760
00:32:50,167 --> 00:32:52,167
- It won't be so
peaceful down there.

761
00:32:52,200 --> 00:32:53,533
- [Tom] Yeah, the grass
is always greener

762
00:32:53,567 --> 00:32:55,400
on the other side of the galaxy.

763
00:32:57,033 --> 00:32:58,767
- [King] You can't trust
young planets.

764
00:32:58,800 --> 00:33:00,033
- What do you mean, admiral?

765
00:33:00,067 --> 00:33:02,067
- [Joel] They're lazy and
they listen to loud music.

766
00:33:02,100 --> 00:33:04,833
- Including things
completely unnoticed.

767
00:33:04,867 --> 00:33:07,067
- Hasn't this planet ever
been explored?

768
00:33:07,100 --> 00:33:09,733
- [King] Not according
to our galactic records.

769
00:33:09,767 --> 00:33:11,133
- [Crow] But then I
couldn't read 'em

770
00:33:11,167 --> 00:33:12,300
'cause I spilled coffee on 'em.

771
00:33:12,333 --> 00:33:14,733
- No sign of life of any kind,
admiral.

772
00:33:14,767 --> 00:33:15,733
Human or otherwise.

773
00:33:16,767 --> 00:33:18,900
- Creatures on these
planets are deceiving.

774
00:33:20,367 --> 00:33:23,833
Even on the ground, you can't
always trust what you see.

775
00:33:23,867 --> 00:33:26,500
- [Joel] Bill, how do you
fight your panty line?

776
00:33:27,600 --> 00:33:28,400
- [Crow] Huh?

777
00:33:28,433 --> 00:33:29,433
Oh, that's man talk.

778
00:33:29,467 --> 00:33:30,733
We'll never understand it.

779
00:33:30,767 --> 00:33:32,133
- 18 years is a long time.

780
00:33:33,333 --> 00:33:34,867
And they couldn't have picked
a worse place to crash.

781
00:33:34,900 --> 00:33:37,733
- [Crow] He says that like
there's a good place to crash.

782
00:33:38,900 --> 00:33:41,233
- Certainly a
botanist's paradise.

783
00:33:41,267 --> 00:33:42,400
- [Joel] I hate to tell
you this, Phil,

784
00:33:42,433 --> 00:33:45,900
but all your aquarium
fish are dead.

785
00:33:45,933 --> 00:33:48,667
- About five million years ago.

786
00:33:48,700 --> 00:33:53,700
Doctor, could man exist
in that environment?

787
00:33:57,467 --> 00:33:58,933
- Probably.

788
00:33:58,967 --> 00:34:02,467
- [Tom] Let's all speak
in broken sentences.

789
00:34:02,500 --> 00:34:05,567
- I think it would be mostly
combating the elements,

790
00:34:05,600 --> 00:34:08,633
defending himself from
who-knows-what.

791
00:34:09,733 --> 00:34:11,933
There could be some
rather ferocious beasts

792
00:34:11,967 --> 00:34:13,633
roaming about that terrain.

793
00:34:13,667 --> 00:34:15,367
- [Crow] Are the scenes
just as static

794
00:34:15,400 --> 00:34:16,633
down on the planet, Bill?

795
00:34:19,300 --> 00:34:22,233
- Inform them we are going to
make a landing on this planet.

796
00:34:22,267 --> 00:34:23,800
- [Tom] Use the good stationery.

797
00:34:24,967 --> 00:34:25,767
- [Joel] Yep.

798
00:34:25,800 --> 00:34:26,600
- That big canyon.

799
00:34:26,633 --> 00:34:27,433
- [Joel] Uh-huh.

800
00:34:27,467 --> 00:34:28,267
- Beyond the jungle.

801
00:34:28,300 --> 00:34:29,700
- [Joel] Yeah, I see it.

802
00:34:29,733 --> 00:34:30,800
- That's your landing site.

803
00:34:30,833 --> 00:34:32,500
- [Tom] Oh.

804
00:34:32,533 --> 00:34:33,800
- Sergeant Alan.

805
00:34:33,833 --> 00:34:34,633
- [Joel] Yep?

806
00:34:34,667 --> 00:34:36,033
Gotcha.

807
00:34:36,067 --> 00:34:37,600
Who should I tell
these orders to?

808
00:34:37,633 --> 00:34:38,900
- Attention all personnel.

809
00:34:38,933 --> 00:34:39,800
Landing stations.

810
00:34:41,967 --> 00:34:43,667
Stand by gravitators.

811
00:34:43,700 --> 00:34:45,600
- Maneuvering room, stand
by gravitators.

812
00:34:45,633 --> 00:34:48,767
- Manuevering room ready
and standing by.

813
00:34:48,800 --> 00:34:50,200
- [Tom] Thanks, Angel.

814
00:34:50,233 --> 00:34:52,200
- I hate to say it,
lieutenant, but I got a feeling

815
00:34:52,233 --> 00:34:55,133
the old man's got a bad
case of cosmic fever.

816
00:34:55,167 --> 00:34:56,667
- [Crow] Well I've got some
salve in my footlocker.

817
00:34:56,700 --> 00:34:57,900
- Where's your spirit of
adventure, chief?

818
00:34:57,933 --> 00:34:59,167
I thought you loved this life.

819
00:34:59,200 --> 00:35:01,600
- Spirit I've got,
adventure I've had.

820
00:35:01,633 --> 00:35:04,000
Love, I was looking forward to.

821
00:35:04,033 --> 00:35:06,133
- I know what you mean, chief.

822
00:35:06,167 --> 00:35:08,567
Look at the words of that
great planeteering prophet.

823
00:35:08,600 --> 00:35:09,767
- Yeah, what'd he say?

824
00:35:09,800 --> 00:35:10,967
- He said, "Let them that
don't want none

825
00:35:11,000 --> 00:35:12,900
"have memories of..."

826
00:35:12,933 --> 00:35:13,900
Forget it.

827
00:35:13,933 --> 00:35:15,067
(laughing)

828
00:35:15,100 --> 00:35:16,200
- [Joel] Great prophet, hope
you didn't get any of that

829
00:35:16,233 --> 00:35:17,900
tattooed anyplace important.

830
00:35:20,600 --> 00:35:22,700
- [Tom] Hey, I see a spot,
let's pull up over there.

831
00:35:22,733 --> 00:35:25,600
(eerie humming)

832
00:35:25,633 --> 00:35:29,233
(instrumental theme music)

833
00:35:33,567 --> 00:35:34,567
- All right, let's take a break.

834
00:35:34,600 --> 00:35:35,733
Go easy on the water.

835
00:35:35,767 --> 00:35:37,467
- [Joel] It
eliminates rest stops.

836
00:35:39,900 --> 00:35:42,333
- Everyone take one
oxygenian tablet.

837
00:35:42,367 --> 00:35:43,200
No more.

838
00:35:44,533 --> 00:35:46,233
- [Crow] I didn't
say Simon Says.

839
00:35:46,267 --> 00:35:48,200
- Like breathing underwater,
hot water.

840
00:35:48,233 --> 00:35:49,633
- You'll get used to it.

841
00:35:49,667 --> 00:35:51,167
- [Tom] It's like being
in the crew's quarters.

842
00:35:51,200 --> 00:35:53,767
- Imagine having to live
in an inferno like this.

843
00:35:53,800 --> 00:35:55,700
- It's probably not too
bad up in the highlands.

844
00:35:56,667 --> 00:35:58,467
- This planet's not too
unlike Centaurus.

845
00:35:58,500 --> 00:36:02,133
- [Joel] Apart from the fact
that it's completely different.

846
00:36:02,167 --> 00:36:03,800
- I imagine the
Centaurians could adapt

847
00:36:03,833 --> 00:36:05,367
to this planet very easily.

848
00:36:05,400 --> 00:36:07,233
- With all this vegetation?

849
00:36:07,267 --> 00:36:08,800
No, they like the deserts, doc.

850
00:36:09,967 --> 00:36:12,433
You give them barren,
windswept oceans of sand--

851
00:36:12,467 --> 00:36:13,733
- [All] Shut up!

852
00:36:13,767 --> 00:36:14,700
- Say, doc.

853
00:36:14,733 --> 00:36:16,567
- [Crow] Do you think I'll
be offed first?

854
00:36:16,600 --> 00:36:18,467
- I mean, Mr. Farrell.

855
00:36:18,500 --> 00:36:20,700
Old Jung says that in the
three months it took us

856
00:36:20,733 --> 00:36:24,367
to get back to this planet,
18 years passed by here.

857
00:36:25,600 --> 00:36:27,000
How does he figure that?

858
00:36:27,033 --> 00:36:28,367
- [Joel] He was kidding!

859
00:36:28,400 --> 00:36:31,433
- I told you half a dozen
times, it's the time paradox.

860
00:36:31,467 --> 00:36:32,533
What's the matter with you?

861
00:36:32,567 --> 00:36:34,767
- [Joel] Oh yeah, I
missed that day.

862
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:36,233
- I still don't see it.

863
00:36:36,267 --> 00:36:37,867
- It's a matter of
reference points.

864
00:36:37,900 --> 00:36:39,700
- [Crow] Ah, it's too
complicated for you, bonehead.

865
00:36:39,733 --> 00:36:41,133
- On our ship we were
traveling at one speed.

866
00:36:41,167 --> 00:36:43,033
This planet travels at another.

867
00:36:43,067 --> 00:36:44,233
- You get it, kid?

868
00:36:44,267 --> 00:36:46,267
For three months, we've
been barreling along

869
00:36:46,300 --> 00:36:47,967
at near the speed of light.

870
00:36:48,833 --> 00:36:51,000
- Yeah, yeah, I know that.

871
00:36:51,033 --> 00:36:51,833
But I--

872
00:36:51,867 --> 00:36:53,100
- Look, look.

873
00:36:53,133 --> 00:36:57,800
This planet rotates on its axis
at only 1,000 miles an hour.

874
00:36:57,833 --> 00:36:59,933
Now that speed
determines the length

875
00:36:59,967 --> 00:37:02,400
of the day, the month and
the year here.

876
00:37:02,433 --> 00:37:03,467
- We gettin' through?

877
00:37:03,500 --> 00:37:04,967
- [Tom] Why don't you
come up to my room tonight

878
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:06,333
and I'll explain it to you?

879
00:37:07,533 --> 00:37:10,167
- Look, at the speed we
were traveling in space

880
00:37:10,200 --> 00:37:14,500
for three months, that was
the equivalent of 6,500--

881
00:37:14,533 --> 00:37:19,500
- [Joel] La la la la la,
can't hear you.

882
00:37:19,533 --> 00:37:21,533
La la la la la la la.

883
00:37:21,567 --> 00:37:23,200
- Yeah, sure.

884
00:37:23,233 --> 00:37:24,200
That's simple.

885
00:37:24,233 --> 00:37:26,600
It's just a matter of
reference points.

886
00:37:27,433 --> 00:37:28,567
Anybody can see that.

887
00:37:28,600 --> 00:37:29,767
- [Crow] He's bluffing.

888
00:37:31,333 --> 00:37:32,767
- [Tom] He's a twit.

889
00:37:32,800 --> 00:37:34,233
- See anything?

890
00:37:34,267 --> 00:37:35,467
- A few birds.

891
00:37:35,500 --> 00:37:36,333
Nothing else.

892
00:37:37,533 --> 00:37:39,667
What do you expect to see,
a welcoming committee?

893
00:37:39,700 --> 00:37:41,000
- Don't get funny.

894
00:37:41,033 --> 00:37:42,533
- [Tom] Don't worry, he won't.

895
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:46,067
- You hear something, chief?

896
00:37:46,100 --> 00:37:48,867
- [Joel] I don't think it's
the welcoming committee.

897
00:37:48,900 --> 00:37:50,533
- Something walking
around up there.

898
00:37:50,567 --> 00:37:51,733
- [Crow] Something big.

899
00:37:54,067 --> 00:37:55,100
- Don't anybody move.

900
00:37:57,600 --> 00:38:00,800
- [Tom] Oh my god, it's an
insert shot of an iguana!

901
00:38:00,833 --> 00:38:03,167
- [Joel] Their technology must
be light years ahead of ours!

902
00:38:03,200 --> 00:38:05,167
Their use of stock
footage is amazing!

903
00:38:07,667 --> 00:38:09,867
Oh great, that's your
answer to everything.

904
00:38:09,900 --> 00:38:11,567
- [Crow] How do you like
your lizard done, boys?

905
00:38:11,600 --> 00:38:13,433
- [Tom] I never knew lizards
were so darn flammable.

906
00:38:13,467 --> 00:38:15,000
- [Joel] No thunder
lizards were hurt

907
00:38:15,033 --> 00:38:17,300
during the filming of this film.

908
00:38:17,333 --> 00:38:18,667
- [Crow] Mmm, extra crispy.

909
00:38:22,400 --> 00:38:23,200
- Dried out?

910
00:38:23,233 --> 00:38:24,500
- [Tom] Sure, can I
go change now?

911
00:38:24,533 --> 00:38:26,433
- Yeah, I think so.

912
00:38:26,467 --> 00:38:28,300
- [Tom] I soiled myself.

913
00:38:28,333 --> 00:38:29,300
- What is it, Alan?

914
00:38:30,567 --> 00:38:32,667
- I can't find a heartbeat.

915
00:38:32,700 --> 00:38:34,833
- Nothing like a little
adventure, eh lieutenant?

916
00:38:34,867 --> 00:38:35,667
- [Joel] Try lower.

917
00:38:35,700 --> 00:38:37,467
- Set up a beamer here.

918
00:38:37,500 --> 00:38:38,333
- [Joel] BMW?

919
00:38:43,667 --> 00:38:45,000
- Cosmos One, this is Scott.

920
00:38:45,033 --> 00:38:45,833
Do you receive me?

921
00:38:45,867 --> 00:38:46,667
- [Crow] Gutless One,
we read you.

922
00:38:46,700 --> 00:38:48,233
- We're receiving you,
commander.

923
00:38:48,267 --> 00:38:50,100
Stevens standing by.

924
00:38:50,133 --> 00:38:51,833
- Ensign, inform the
admiral that I advise

925
00:38:51,867 --> 00:38:53,133
no one be allowed to
leave the ship

926
00:38:53,167 --> 00:38:54,433
without being well-armed.

927
00:38:55,467 --> 00:38:56,700
- Scott, this is King.

928
00:38:56,733 --> 00:38:58,700
- [Tom] Are you speaking
into a Water Pik?

929
00:38:58,733 --> 00:38:59,800
- We've encountered one of those

930
00:38:59,833 --> 00:39:03,700
deceptive creatures you
mentioned, a giant lizard.

931
00:39:03,733 --> 00:39:04,900
It's been destroyed but I'm sure

932
00:39:04,933 --> 00:39:07,133
there are others in this area.

933
00:39:07,167 --> 00:39:09,500
We're about halfway to the
crash site now, admiral.

934
00:39:09,533 --> 00:39:11,600
I'll leave a beamer at
this location.

935
00:39:11,633 --> 00:39:12,733
That's all, sir.

936
00:39:12,767 --> 00:39:14,433
- Very well, Mr. Scott.

937
00:39:14,467 --> 00:39:16,700
Carry on and keep a sharp watch.

938
00:39:16,733 --> 00:39:18,933
Don't want to be caught
with your guard down.

939
00:39:18,967 --> 00:39:19,800
- Yes, sir.

940
00:39:21,633 --> 00:39:23,333
- Very well, Mr. Scott,
carry on.

941
00:39:23,367 --> 00:39:24,867
Keep a sharp watch.

942
00:39:24,900 --> 00:39:27,267
You don't want to be caught
with your guard down.

943
00:39:27,300 --> 00:39:29,267
- [Joel] Stop doing
your Cagney impression,

944
00:39:29,300 --> 00:39:31,167
it's not that great.

945
00:39:31,200 --> 00:39:33,300
- My commanding officer
asked for volunteers

946
00:39:33,333 --> 00:39:35,467
for an important expedition.

947
00:39:35,500 --> 00:39:37,167
I thought he meant exhibition.

948
00:39:37,200 --> 00:39:39,833
- [Crow] Yeah, and my uncle's
the producer on the film, too.

949
00:39:39,867 --> 00:39:41,633
- All right men, let's move.

950
00:39:41,667 --> 00:39:42,933
And keep a sharp watch.

951
00:39:45,067 --> 00:39:47,033
- [Joel] It's our first
Christmas on the planet

952
00:39:47,067 --> 00:39:48,600
and you've been just grand.

953
00:39:50,800 --> 00:39:52,133
We'd better go be with
the others now.

954
00:39:52,167 --> 00:39:53,733
- If that's where they
grow lizards around here,

955
00:39:53,767 --> 00:39:56,167
I'd hate to run into a snake.

956
00:39:57,133 --> 00:39:59,267
- [Joel] Good one.

957
00:39:59,300 --> 00:40:00,300
- [Tom] There's a
well on the ship.

958
00:40:00,333 --> 00:40:01,100
(admiral mumbling)

959
00:40:01,133 --> 00:40:01,967
- [Joel] What?

960
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:03,900
- Sorry men, your
liberty's canceled.

961
00:40:03,933 --> 00:40:06,400
No one is to leave the ship
under any circumstances.

962
00:40:06,433 --> 00:40:08,267
- Have the located the
Cosmos Three, sir?

963
00:40:08,300 --> 00:40:09,767
- Not yet.

964
00:40:09,800 --> 00:40:12,233
- Well there goes the ball game,
huh?

965
00:40:12,267 --> 00:40:13,567
- They must have run
into trouble out there.

966
00:40:13,600 --> 00:40:14,600
- I wish I was with 'em.

967
00:40:14,633 --> 00:40:16,233
- Anything would be
better than being stuck in

968
00:40:16,267 --> 00:40:18,033
this king-sized
community capsule.

969
00:40:18,067 --> 00:40:18,867
- [Crow] Oh, you.

970
00:40:18,900 --> 00:40:20,033
- Admiral King!

971
00:40:20,067 --> 00:40:21,733
Linda is out of the ship.

972
00:40:21,767 --> 00:40:22,733
- Are you sure?

973
00:40:22,767 --> 00:40:25,967
- She said she wished to
breathe the fresh air,

974
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:28,233
and feel the warm of the sun.

975
00:40:28,267 --> 00:40:31,067
- [Tom] Just tell me where
she went, Hemingway, come on.

976
00:40:32,200 --> 00:40:33,500
- She's been dying to
get off this ship

977
00:40:33,533 --> 00:40:34,600
ever since we landed.

978
00:40:36,733 --> 00:40:39,333
- [Crow] Will it help if I
strike a pose right here?

979
00:40:43,833 --> 00:40:44,800
- Harris, get my field gear.

980
00:40:44,833 --> 00:40:47,033
- [Joel] And my spare pants.

981
00:40:47,067 --> 00:40:49,800
- Admiral King, you can't
take this chance, sir.

982
00:40:49,833 --> 00:40:52,733
If anything should happen
to you or Commander Scott,

983
00:40:52,767 --> 00:40:53,967
this ship would never
leave this planet.

984
00:40:54,000 --> 00:40:56,100
- [Tom] Yes, you'd be in
charge, yes, I realize that.

985
00:40:57,100 --> 00:40:59,033
- Harris, you and Wilson
go look for her.

986
00:40:59,067 --> 00:41:00,500
- She's probably near the ship.

987
00:41:00,533 --> 00:41:01,367
- Yes, sir.

988
00:41:01,400 --> 00:41:02,567
- Bring laser rifles with you.

989
00:41:02,600 --> 00:41:05,100
- [Crow] I'll stay here
and take more lithium.

990
00:41:05,133 --> 00:41:05,933
- Yes, sir.

991
00:41:05,967 --> 00:41:06,767
- Don't worry, admiral.

992
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:07,667
We'll find her.

993
00:41:07,700 --> 00:41:09,533
- [Tom] Spin and Marty
to the rescue!

994
00:41:10,767 --> 00:41:12,133
- Poor Linda.

995
00:41:12,167 --> 00:41:13,833
She's such a lost child.

996
00:41:15,733 --> 00:41:18,500
- Karen, if anything
happens to her,

997
00:41:18,533 --> 00:41:20,700
I'll never forgive myself.

998
00:41:22,067 --> 00:41:23,600
- I understand.

999
00:41:23,633 --> 00:41:24,600
- She's just like her mother.

1000
00:41:24,633 --> 00:41:26,900
- [Tom] Oh Ward, the
Beaver turned out okay.

1001
00:41:28,533 --> 00:41:31,600
- Filled with childlike
dreams of another world.

1002
00:41:31,633 --> 00:41:33,733
- [Joel] What is he, Anne of
Green Gables all of a sudden?

1003
00:41:33,767 --> 00:41:34,567
Hey!

1004
00:41:34,600 --> 00:41:35,567
- Cannot be changed.

1005
00:41:36,567 --> 00:41:38,733
(beeping)

1006
00:41:40,533 --> 00:41:41,833
- [Crow] What did he want?

1007
00:41:44,067 --> 00:41:46,400
- I didn't know he knew
Linda's mother.

1008
00:41:46,433 --> 00:41:49,267
I thought she was killed in
the Centaurian tribal war.

1009
00:41:49,300 --> 00:41:54,100
- It is true, but the admiral
knew her long before that.

1010
00:41:54,133 --> 00:41:58,400
He made many expeditions into
the desert in those years.

1011
00:41:58,433 --> 00:41:59,367
- [Crow] Oh wait a minute,
wait a minute.

1012
00:41:59,400 --> 00:42:01,133
You're describing the
plot of Kung-Fu.

1013
00:42:01,167 --> 00:42:02,133
- Who was Linda's father?

1014
00:42:02,167 --> 00:42:03,567
- [Tom] We better get
out of here.

1015
00:42:03,600 --> 00:42:04,467
- [Crow] Oh boy.

1016
00:42:04,500 --> 00:42:05,500
- [Joel] We gotta disarm
that satellite!

1017
00:42:05,533 --> 00:42:06,767
- [Crow] Oh yeah, I wanna help.

1018
00:42:06,800 --> 00:42:08,900
- [Joel] Let's get going.

1019
00:42:11,400 --> 00:42:15,000
(instrumental theme music)

1020
00:42:16,867 --> 00:42:19,200
You know, this makes no
sense at all.

1021
00:42:19,233 --> 00:42:21,467
Whoever heard of a
doomsday machine

1022
00:42:21,500 --> 00:42:23,400
with a fold-lock top in it?

1023
00:42:23,433 --> 00:42:24,733
- Hey, hey Joel, look,

1024
00:42:24,767 --> 00:42:26,733
I found a instruction
manual right there, see?

1025
00:42:26,767 --> 00:42:27,767
- Thanks.

1026
00:42:27,800 --> 00:42:32,000
It says Isaac Asimov
Literary Doomsday Machine.

1027
00:42:32,033 --> 00:42:35,567
It's an instruction manual,
must be over 1,000 pages long.

1028
00:42:35,600 --> 00:42:36,700
How typical.

1029
00:42:36,733 --> 00:42:38,133
- Literary doomsday?

1030
00:42:38,167 --> 00:42:39,600
Isn't that when your
library fines

1031
00:42:39,633 --> 00:42:41,133
exceed the price of the book?

1032
00:42:41,167 --> 00:42:43,633
- I thought it was every
time Jackie Collins

1033
00:42:43,667 --> 00:42:45,000
makes it to the
best-seller list.

1034
00:42:45,033 --> 00:42:46,567
- Oh, settle down,
you goonheads.

1035
00:42:46,600 --> 00:42:48,800
We got this doomsday
machine to disarm,

1036
00:42:48,833 --> 00:42:50,367
and well, we gotta
check the manual.

1037
00:42:50,400 --> 00:42:51,633
Let's see.

1038
00:42:51,667 --> 00:42:54,933
It looks like it's translated
from the Korean or something.

1039
00:42:54,967 --> 00:42:58,100
- They must have sub-contracted
the satellite for him.

1040
00:42:58,133 --> 00:43:01,033
- I don't get it, Asimov
must have gone mad.

1041
00:43:01,067 --> 00:43:02,700
Why would anyone want to
make a doomsday machine?

1042
00:43:02,733 --> 00:43:04,967
- Well he's probably
mad because no one else

1043
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:07,300
is as smart as him, or
else that L. Ron Hubbard

1044
00:43:07,333 --> 00:43:08,833
has more followers than him.

1045
00:43:08,867 --> 00:43:10,600
- Well, didn't Asimov
try to establish

1046
00:43:10,633 --> 00:43:12,367
the Church of the
Super Quiz once?

1047
00:43:12,400 --> 00:43:14,267
- Oh knock it off, you
spinach-chins.

1048
00:43:14,300 --> 00:43:15,933
I gotta read this manual.

1049
00:43:15,967 --> 00:43:20,500
Step one, it will be very
enjoyable for you to separate

1050
00:43:20,533 --> 00:43:24,867
the ocular filter coupling
of from the decapacitor

1051
00:43:25,767 --> 00:43:29,600
which is stout and yellow,
sometimes.

1052
00:43:29,633 --> 00:43:32,233
Crow you'd better scan this
and give me the instructions.

1053
00:43:32,267 --> 00:43:33,333
(high-pitched whirring)

1054
00:43:33,367 --> 00:43:34,200
- Got it!

1055
00:43:35,267 --> 00:43:39,633
Okay, most very kindly,
find the looky switch

1056
00:43:39,667 --> 00:43:40,967
which is nice and sitting there

1057
00:43:41,000 --> 00:43:43,900
with green label that
leaves you singing.

1058
00:43:43,933 --> 00:43:45,167
- I think I got it.

1059
00:43:46,767 --> 00:43:49,033
- Okay, carefully
disregard and do not do

1060
00:43:49,067 --> 00:43:51,867
the very wrong thing or
much confusion will result.

1061
00:43:51,900 --> 00:43:52,967
Tell me about it.

1062
00:43:53,000 --> 00:43:56,667
With sparks, flowers and
loud report on some models.

1063
00:43:56,700 --> 00:44:00,700
Glue Batman to seat G,
detail omitted for clarity?

1064
00:44:00,733 --> 00:44:02,733
- This is really confusing.

1065
00:44:02,767 --> 00:44:04,667
- Who wrote this,
Charlie Callas?

1066
00:44:06,767 --> 00:44:08,500
- Hey, oh, oh, wait,
there's more.

1067
00:44:08,533 --> 00:44:12,467
It says clip red wire,
likes you best

1068
00:44:12,500 --> 00:44:14,933
with firm hand and glad heart.

1069
00:44:14,967 --> 00:44:15,933
- Okay.

1070
00:44:15,967 --> 00:44:17,800
I think that oughta do it.

1071
00:44:17,833 --> 00:44:21,000
- But first, clip the blue wire.

1072
00:44:21,033 --> 00:44:23,033
(evil mechanical laughing)

1073
00:44:23,067 --> 00:44:24,067
That's what it said.

1074
00:44:24,100 --> 00:44:25,033
(alarms blaring)

1075
00:44:25,067 --> 00:44:26,433
- Oh man, we got movie sign.

1076
00:44:26,467 --> 00:44:28,267
(all yelling)

1077
00:44:28,300 --> 00:44:31,467
(mechanical whirring)

1078
00:44:39,900 --> 00:44:41,433
- [Joel] (groaning) My eyes.

1079
00:44:42,367 --> 00:44:44,133
- [Tom] You got creamed.

1080
00:44:45,300 --> 00:44:46,133
You okay?

1081
00:44:54,000 --> 00:44:54,800
- [Joel] Say!

1082
00:44:54,833 --> 00:44:55,633
(screaming)

1083
00:44:55,667 --> 00:44:58,033
Seems like a nice little booger,
aah!

1084
00:44:58,067 --> 00:45:00,300
- [Crow] Are you chafing
like a bear or is it just me?

1085
00:45:00,333 --> 00:45:01,400
- I don't know, it sounded
like a bird call to me.

1086
00:45:01,433 --> 00:45:04,067
- [Crow] Sounded like a
girl screaming at a snake.

1087
00:45:06,633 --> 00:45:09,133
- [Joel] Hey, the snake
pushed her into the river.

1088
00:45:11,033 --> 00:45:13,700
- [Tom] Fortunately I have
my Johnny Rocket crossbow.

1089
00:45:15,967 --> 00:45:17,267
- [Crow] Snake on a stake.

1090
00:45:20,300 --> 00:45:21,867
- [Tom] Hey, look what
someone threw back.

1091
00:45:21,900 --> 00:45:23,900
Cool, this'll look great
over the mantel.

1092
00:45:23,933 --> 00:45:25,700
I can't believe, this
is a keeper.

1093
00:45:29,300 --> 00:45:31,600
- [Crow] Hey, watch those hands.

1094
00:45:31,633 --> 00:45:33,833
- [Tom] Amazing what you
find if you just look.

1095
00:45:36,467 --> 00:45:38,500
- [Joel] She'll be perfect
for my experiments.

1096
00:45:38,533 --> 00:45:40,700
- [Crow] And Quincy
will be so proud of me.

1097
00:45:44,100 --> 00:45:48,267
- [Joel] Say, this hotel's
got everything.

1098
00:45:48,300 --> 00:45:49,900
I wonder where the game room is.

1099
00:46:02,933 --> 00:46:05,167
- Get a load of this place,
will ya?

1100
00:46:05,200 --> 00:46:06,933
You're looking at
Paradise Island.

1101
00:46:06,967 --> 00:46:08,233
- [Joel] I hear ya, pal.

1102
00:46:09,400 --> 00:46:10,800
- Also the end of the trail,

1103
00:46:11,667 --> 00:46:13,467
unless you're a mountain goat.

1104
00:46:13,500 --> 00:46:15,800
- [Joel] Well, I used to be.

1105
00:46:15,833 --> 00:46:17,767
- I think we missed her.

1106
00:46:17,800 --> 00:46:19,400
- Maybe she's back
there someplace.

1107
00:46:24,067 --> 00:46:24,900
- Tracks.

1108
00:46:25,867 --> 00:46:27,567
She's been right around
here someplace.

1109
00:46:27,600 --> 00:46:30,467
- [Crow] Like right where
these tracks were made?

1110
00:46:30,500 --> 00:46:32,967
- Do you think she fell in?

1111
00:46:33,000 --> 00:46:35,900
I mean, do Centaurians
know how to swim?

1112
00:46:38,567 --> 00:46:39,400
- I don't know.

1113
00:46:44,800 --> 00:46:45,633
Her boot!

1114
00:46:46,733 --> 00:46:47,933
- [Crow] Dibs, dibs!

1115
00:46:47,967 --> 00:46:50,467
Let me drink champagne out
of it, just to be sure.

1116
00:46:53,967 --> 00:46:55,533
- Look at the size
of that thing.

1117
00:46:55,567 --> 00:46:57,500
- [Joel] Oh, I've seen
trees bigger than that.

1118
00:46:57,533 --> 00:46:58,567
That's nothing.

1119
00:46:58,600 --> 00:46:59,400
- Let's get back to the ship.

1120
00:46:59,433 --> 00:47:01,367
Let's go, come on, come on,
come on.

1121
00:47:04,700 --> 00:47:06,333
- [Tom] We've been pacing
this studio for hours.

1122
00:47:06,367 --> 00:47:08,267
When do we get some
action happening?

1123
00:47:22,700 --> 00:47:27,367
- [Crow] Hmm, coconut cream
pie, car made out of bamboo,

1124
00:47:27,933 --> 00:47:29,333
and a sailor's hat.

1125
00:47:29,367 --> 00:47:30,567
What's it all mean?

1126
00:47:38,067 --> 00:47:39,333
- All right, let's take five.

1127
00:47:39,367 --> 00:47:40,500
- [Tom] One, two, three, four,
five.

1128
00:47:40,533 --> 00:47:41,400
(laughing) Psych!

1129
00:47:48,133 --> 00:47:48,967
- What's the matter, Bradley?

1130
00:47:49,000 --> 00:47:50,467
This hike too much for you?

1131
00:47:50,500 --> 00:47:53,100
- Oh no doc, I always
enjoy a 40-mile walk

1132
00:47:53,133 --> 00:47:54,467
on a lovely day like this.

1133
00:47:55,567 --> 00:47:57,467
- [Crow] You ever see the
movie Alive, donut boy?

1134
00:47:57,500 --> 00:47:59,567
- You were 10 pounds overweight.

1135
00:48:00,600 --> 00:48:01,467
- Are you kiddin', doc?

1136
00:48:01,500 --> 00:48:03,133
I've been on a diet
for seven days,

1137
00:48:03,167 --> 00:48:05,300
and so far all I lost is a week.

1138
00:48:05,333 --> 00:48:06,267
- [Joel] Good one.

1139
00:48:06,300 --> 00:48:08,233
- [Tom] And your
self-respect, for that joke.

1140
00:48:08,267 --> 00:48:09,667
- That's the story of my life.

1141
00:48:09,700 --> 00:48:12,033
I'm always volunteering
for something.

1142
00:48:12,067 --> 00:48:13,667
I remember one time back
at headquarters,

1143
00:48:13,700 --> 00:48:15,733
I volunteered for a
karate course.

1144
00:48:15,767 --> 00:48:17,600
They taught me all the hits,
the chops,

1145
00:48:17,633 --> 00:48:19,400
the head, the neck, the
shoulders, the stomach.

1146
00:48:19,433 --> 00:48:20,733
The karate kicks, hah!

1147
00:48:20,767 --> 00:48:22,500
- [Crow] Who are you,
Donald O'Connor?

1148
00:48:22,533 --> 00:48:23,633
- Hi-keeba, hah!

1149
00:48:25,800 --> 00:48:27,733
- [Tom] You know, I
could watch that all day.

1150
00:48:27,767 --> 00:48:29,567
Do that again, will ya?

1151
00:48:29,600 --> 00:48:31,867
- And after
completing the course,

1152
00:48:31,900 --> 00:48:33,733
I became a karate expert.

1153
00:48:33,767 --> 00:48:35,367
- [Joel] When did he
become an idiot?

1154
00:48:35,400 --> 00:48:38,333
- I went around breaking
boards with my bare hands.

1155
00:48:38,367 --> 00:48:40,267
The first time I
saluted Admiral King,

1156
00:48:41,367 --> 00:48:42,733
I almost knocked my brains out.

1157
00:48:42,767 --> 00:48:43,567
- [Crow] Sure you
didn't succeed?

1158
00:48:43,600 --> 00:48:45,533
- For this, this
mission to Centaurus

1159
00:48:45,567 --> 00:48:47,200
and look where it got me.

1160
00:48:47,233 --> 00:48:48,700
- Like you always told me,
lieutenant,

1161
00:48:48,733 --> 00:48:50,400
where's your spirit
of adventure?

1162
00:48:50,433 --> 00:48:51,767
- [Tom] I left it in
my other pants.

1163
00:48:51,800 --> 00:48:55,600
- That's what makes all of
this worthwhile, the adventure.

1164
00:48:55,633 --> 00:48:58,267
Day after day, week after
week, month after month.

1165
00:48:58,300 --> 00:49:00,833
Year after year, oh the
sheer thrill of it all.

1166
00:49:00,867 --> 00:49:04,167
Perusing the planets,
unifying the universe.

1167
00:49:04,200 --> 00:49:06,100
Galloping through the galactics.

1168
00:49:06,133 --> 00:49:06,967
- [All] Shut up!

1169
00:49:10,800 --> 00:49:11,800
- We'd landed our ship
in the middle of

1170
00:49:11,833 --> 00:49:13,367
the densest part of the jungle.

1171
00:49:13,400 --> 00:49:15,133
We were about 200 yards
from the ship--

1172
00:49:15,167 --> 00:49:17,233
- [Crow] Morty Gunty,
appearing this week at

1173
00:49:17,267 --> 00:49:20,233
the Blaine Community Theater
in Shakespeare's King Lear.

1174
00:49:21,467 --> 00:49:25,100
- With fire and flame shooting
out of all three nostrils.

1175
00:49:25,133 --> 00:49:27,167
Well, I raised my laser gun.

1176
00:49:27,200 --> 00:49:29,367
- [Crow] Shut him up.

1177
00:49:29,400 --> 00:49:31,133
- But the gun wouldn't work.

1178
00:49:31,167 --> 00:49:33,100
It looked like certain
death for all of us.

1179
00:49:33,133 --> 00:49:34,600
- [Joel] I can't reach his nose.

1180
00:49:34,633 --> 00:49:36,967
- I reached back and I
grabbed a handful of yours,

1181
00:49:37,000 --> 00:49:38,667
and I threw it right in the
beast's face and killed it.

1182
00:49:38,700 --> 00:49:39,967
- Now, just a minute Red.

1183
00:49:41,033 --> 00:49:43,433
You reached back and
grabbed a handful of what?

1184
00:49:43,467 --> 00:49:44,933
- Yours, a handful of yours.

1185
00:49:44,967 --> 00:49:45,767
And I threw it right in his--

1186
00:49:45,800 --> 00:49:47,700
- Okay, okay, Bradley, tell me.

1187
00:49:47,733 --> 00:49:48,900
What's yours?

1188
00:49:48,933 --> 00:49:50,233
- I'll have a three-day pass,
sir.

1189
00:49:50,267 --> 00:49:52,267
(groaning)

1190
00:49:52,300 --> 00:49:53,433
- [Tom] Ba-ba-boom!

1191
00:49:53,467 --> 00:49:55,267
(goofy laughing)

1192
00:49:55,300 --> 00:49:57,500
- Let's move out, shall we?

1193
00:49:57,533 --> 00:49:58,967
- [Crow] He'll be
riding in the trunk

1194
00:49:59,000 --> 00:50:01,033
on the way back to Earth.

1195
00:50:01,067 --> 00:50:02,867
- [Joel] He's a real
child of hell.

1196
00:50:06,867 --> 00:50:09,633
(dramatic music)

1197
00:50:14,467 --> 00:50:16,967
I gotta get a new log
out here or somethin'.

1198
00:50:17,000 --> 00:50:19,933
(animal squeaking)

1199
00:50:29,267 --> 00:50:30,700
- [Crow] Ah Wilma, you're up.

1200
00:50:40,267 --> 00:50:42,233
- [Joel] Have you met Steve,
my monkey?

1201
00:50:45,533 --> 00:50:46,500
- [Tom] You got some
flaking there.

1202
00:50:46,533 --> 00:50:48,100
Maybe you could use a henna.

1203
00:50:50,000 --> 00:50:50,833
- Pretty girl.

1204
00:50:52,767 --> 00:50:53,933
- Who are you?

1205
00:50:55,333 --> 00:50:56,500
- I am Tang.

1206
00:50:56,533 --> 00:50:58,167
- [Tom] I'm not just
for breakfast anymore.

1207
00:50:58,200 --> 00:50:59,533
- [Joel] That's my
favorite drink!

1208
00:50:59,567 --> 00:51:02,100
- [Crow] It's short for
Australopithecus Africanus.

1209
00:51:02,133 --> 00:51:03,300
- I am Centaurian.

1210
00:51:04,300 --> 00:51:06,033
- [Joel] Tang is my
favorite drink.

1211
00:51:07,400 --> 00:51:09,467
- You are Centaurian.

1212
00:51:09,500 --> 00:51:10,433
We are safe.

1213
00:51:13,233 --> 00:51:16,967
- Well how did you get
here, on this planet?

1214
00:51:18,067 --> 00:51:19,167
- This is my homeland.

1215
00:51:22,233 --> 00:51:23,700
- You were born here.

1216
00:51:24,767 --> 00:51:27,100
Your mother was aboard
the Cosmos Three.

1217
00:51:27,133 --> 00:51:29,867
- [Tom] Hey, your mother
swims after troop ships, lady.

1218
00:51:31,100 --> 00:51:32,133
- Survivors?

1219
00:51:33,033 --> 00:51:35,333
- Yes, your mother and father.

1220
00:51:36,433 --> 00:51:37,267
Where are they?

1221
00:51:39,833 --> 00:51:41,467
- [Joel] Um, you're
wearing them.

1222
00:51:44,833 --> 00:51:46,500
- I will take you to them.

1223
00:51:52,167 --> 00:51:53,167
- Tang?

1224
00:51:53,200 --> 00:51:56,100
- [Crow] Uh, fresh out,
but I got catawba juice.

1225
00:51:56,133 --> 00:51:57,800
- Clothes wet, you
fall in water.

1226
00:51:59,267 --> 00:52:02,100
- Oh yes, I remember.

1227
00:52:02,133 --> 00:52:03,833
- There was a serpent.

1228
00:52:03,867 --> 00:52:05,667
- I killed it, I bring you here.

1229
00:52:05,700 --> 00:52:07,633
- [Joel] This hot stick.

1230
00:52:07,667 --> 00:52:08,867
- [Tom] You'll like 'em.

1231
00:52:12,833 --> 00:52:14,733
Leave the shower curtain here.

1232
00:52:18,233 --> 00:52:19,900
- [Crow] Oh, by the way,
I did that totem pole

1233
00:52:19,933 --> 00:52:21,900
just 'cause I thought I
was supposed to.

1234
00:52:25,167 --> 00:52:26,900
- [Tom] How much per
month for this?

1235
00:52:26,933 --> 00:52:28,900
With the damage deposit?

1236
00:52:36,267 --> 00:52:39,667
(Linda speaking quietly)

1237
00:52:51,467 --> 00:52:53,967
- [Crow] Now, join me
in my dance of death.

1238
00:53:03,767 --> 00:53:05,533
- [Tom] That's cold.

1239
00:53:05,567 --> 00:53:06,900
- It's beautiful.

1240
00:53:06,933 --> 00:53:07,900
- Mother.

1241
00:53:07,933 --> 00:53:09,367
- [Joel] She's not bad,
except for a little

1242
00:53:09,400 --> 00:53:10,933
freezer burn right
around the edges.

1243
00:53:10,967 --> 00:53:12,533
- [Tom] It's Clarence Birdseye.

1244
00:53:12,567 --> 00:53:13,700
- Lieutenant Anderson!

1245
00:53:14,633 --> 00:53:16,467
He's not a Centaurian.

1246
00:53:16,500 --> 00:53:17,433
- My father.

1247
00:53:19,800 --> 00:53:22,333
- [Crow] Well, they're
no bowling trophies.

1248
00:53:22,367 --> 00:53:25,167
- I must tell the
admiral about this.

1249
00:53:25,200 --> 00:53:28,367
I must go back to the
ship that brought me here.

1250
00:53:28,400 --> 00:53:29,733
Do you know where the ship is,
Tang?

1251
00:53:30,867 --> 00:53:33,067
- I know, I take you there.

1252
00:53:33,100 --> 00:53:35,133
- [Crow] And then I'll
get some pronouns.

1253
00:53:41,033 --> 00:53:42,833
Meanwhile, back at the
dry ice pool.

1254
00:53:46,700 --> 00:53:49,367
(pool bubbling)

1255
00:53:56,267 --> 00:53:58,667
- [Tom] Oh, that's just mean.

1256
00:54:01,200 --> 00:54:02,933
- Yeah, they could use a
spare deodorant.

1257
00:54:02,967 --> 00:54:05,667
You rub it on, the smell
stays but you disappear.

1258
00:54:05,700 --> 00:54:06,667
- [Joel] Good one.

1259
00:54:06,700 --> 00:54:09,033
- It's boiling crude oil,
commander.

1260
00:54:09,067 --> 00:54:10,300
- Boy, what a spot for
a steam bath.

1261
00:54:10,333 --> 00:54:12,900
- [Joel] Just cross the
log and you're in the club.

1262
00:54:12,933 --> 00:54:13,933
- Hand me that rope.

1263
00:54:17,133 --> 00:54:18,500
- [Tom] You could walk around.

1264
00:54:19,367 --> 00:54:20,333
- [Crow] Too easy.

1265
00:54:21,967 --> 00:54:25,000
Sure glad the prop boys laid
this log out here for us.

1266
00:54:31,733 --> 00:54:34,100
- [Tom] If the Wallendas
can do it, we can do it.

1267
00:54:34,133 --> 00:54:36,367
- He's got more nerve
than I thought he had.

1268
00:54:36,400 --> 00:54:37,533
- Scott's a good man, Bradley.

1269
00:54:37,567 --> 00:54:39,433
- [Joel] He has wonderful
bone structure,

1270
00:54:39,467 --> 00:54:42,033
great teeth and a
darling figure.

1271
00:54:42,067 --> 00:54:44,433
- Yeah, but what a miserable
place to have to search.

1272
00:54:44,467 --> 00:54:45,967
- [Tom] He's right over there.

1273
00:54:46,000 --> 00:54:48,467
- A hazardous mission is
like a mirror of truth.

1274
00:54:48,500 --> 00:54:51,167
When you face it, you see
your true self.

1275
00:54:52,167 --> 00:54:54,033
- [Crow] Oh shut up,
what are you, Confucius?

1276
00:54:54,067 --> 00:54:56,233
Just cross the dry
ice and shut up!

1277
00:54:58,000 --> 00:54:59,633
- Why don't you build a
better bridge?

1278
00:54:59,667 --> 00:55:00,833
- (chuckling) Wrong
kind of engineers.

1279
00:55:00,867 --> 00:55:03,800
- [Joel] Uh, you see, we
just play with toy trains.

1280
00:55:04,733 --> 00:55:05,633
- Frankly, yeah.

1281
00:55:06,933 --> 00:55:08,233
- Doc, I don't think Alan
better try it.

1282
00:55:08,267 --> 00:55:10,567
- [Tom] Might wanna take
the slack outta that rope.

1283
00:55:10,600 --> 00:55:12,033
- You stay behind.

1284
00:55:12,067 --> 00:55:13,433
- [Crow] You little pantywaist.

1285
00:55:13,467 --> 00:55:15,367
Boy if that was my kid,
I'd whack him.

1286
00:55:17,067 --> 00:55:17,867
- I'm okay, doc.

1287
00:55:17,900 --> 00:55:20,033
If you can make it, I can.

1288
00:55:20,067 --> 00:55:20,967
- Suit yourself.

1289
00:55:22,367 --> 00:55:24,267
- He's got it secure, let's go.

1290
00:55:24,300 --> 00:55:25,600
- [Joel] He's got tequila?

1291
00:55:30,900 --> 00:55:34,067
- [Tom] My blood pressure
is just racing.

1292
00:55:34,100 --> 00:55:38,467
- [Joel] Why don't they
just go around right there?

1293
00:55:38,500 --> 00:55:40,600
(shouting)

1294
00:55:40,633 --> 00:55:43,533
Don't fall, don't fall.

1295
00:55:45,067 --> 00:55:46,567
- [Crow] Jinx, jinx.

1296
00:55:46,600 --> 00:55:47,400
- [Tom] Noonan!

1297
00:55:47,433 --> 00:55:48,267
- [Joel] Noonan.

1298
00:55:49,333 --> 00:55:50,967
- [Crow] Jinx!

1299
00:55:51,000 --> 00:55:55,733
(screaming)
(all groan)

1300
00:55:57,100 --> 00:55:57,900
- [Crow] Hotfoot.

1301
00:55:57,933 --> 00:55:59,667
- [Tom] A gainer, yes it is.

1302
00:55:59,700 --> 00:56:01,867
- [Joel] Well I guess
he's not in the club.

1303
00:56:03,033 --> 00:56:05,500
- [Crow] Never did
like him anyway.

1304
00:56:05,533 --> 00:56:06,367
- You all right?

1305
00:56:06,400 --> 00:56:07,833
- Lousy.

1306
00:56:07,867 --> 00:56:09,367
That's what this
whole mission is.

1307
00:56:09,400 --> 00:56:10,433
- [Tom] Can I have his locker?

1308
00:56:11,467 --> 00:56:13,800
- What the hell are we
trying to prove, anyway?

1309
00:56:13,833 --> 00:56:15,433
Searching this stinkin'
nowhere planet

1310
00:56:15,467 --> 00:56:17,467
for a bunch of survivors
that may not exist?

1311
00:56:17,500 --> 00:56:19,767
- [Crow] Hey, I got
Angelo to think of!

1312
00:56:19,800 --> 00:56:20,900
- Take it easy, chief.

1313
00:56:22,200 --> 00:56:23,633
- Take it easy?

1314
00:56:23,667 --> 00:56:26,633
You watch a man die like that
and you say take it easy?

1315
00:56:26,667 --> 00:56:28,067
- [Joel] Hey, I thought
it was funny.

1316
00:56:28,100 --> 00:56:28,933
Why?

1317
00:56:30,833 --> 00:56:32,700
- You all right now, chief?

1318
00:56:32,733 --> 00:56:33,633
- Yes, sir.

1319
00:56:33,667 --> 00:56:35,667
- [Tom] Yeah, thanks for
not hitting me.

1320
00:56:37,300 --> 00:56:38,900
- Something just happened to me.

1321
00:56:39,967 --> 00:56:41,367
Got a little shook, I guess.

1322
00:56:42,933 --> 00:56:44,233
- Forget it, chief.

1323
00:56:44,267 --> 00:56:45,433
We're all a little shook.

1324
00:56:45,467 --> 00:56:46,700
- [Joel] Dickweed.

1325
00:56:46,733 --> 00:56:48,400
- We're almost there.

1326
00:56:48,433 --> 00:56:49,267
Let's move on.

1327
00:56:50,600 --> 00:56:51,667
- [Tom] Jerk.

1328
00:56:55,400 --> 00:56:56,500
- Come on, son.

1329
00:56:56,533 --> 00:56:57,600
- [Crow] I know how
you're feeling.

1330
00:56:57,633 --> 00:56:58,733
You see this shoulder?

1331
00:56:58,767 --> 00:57:00,067
It's here if you need it.

1332
00:57:01,133 --> 00:57:01,967
Idiot.

1333
00:57:03,500 --> 00:57:04,933
- [Joel] Now would you
go back across the log

1334
00:57:04,967 --> 00:57:06,333
and unhook the rope?

1335
00:57:06,367 --> 00:57:08,600
- [Tom] That makes me hungry.

1336
00:57:08,633 --> 00:57:10,467
- [Joel] Is it
primordial soup yet?

1337
00:57:15,700 --> 00:57:17,267
- [Crow] Now where did we park?

1338
00:57:22,167 --> 00:57:23,733
- [Joel] More of the same.

1339
00:57:23,767 --> 00:57:24,633
Oh brother.

1340
00:57:31,233 --> 00:57:32,467
- [Tom] Whose line is it?

1341
00:57:33,367 --> 00:57:34,867
- [Joel] Somebody.

1342
00:57:42,600 --> 00:57:45,033
(talking over each other)

1343
00:57:45,067 --> 00:57:46,467
- He's trying to
trick me isn't he?

1344
00:57:46,500 --> 00:57:48,033
Nobody could have
survived this crash.

1345
00:57:48,067 --> 00:57:50,067
- Bradley, you and the
chief wait here.

1346
00:57:50,100 --> 00:57:52,800
We can't be sure what
we might find inside.

1347
00:57:52,833 --> 00:57:53,767
You with me, doc?

1348
00:57:55,367 --> 00:57:57,967
- [Joel] Yeah, you two
disposable characters wait here.

1349
00:58:06,333 --> 00:58:10,033
- - [Crow] Wow, looks
like they turned that ship

1350
00:58:10,067 --> 00:58:11,867
into a restaurant.

1351
00:58:11,900 --> 00:58:13,933
I love these fern bars.

1352
00:58:13,967 --> 00:58:16,300
Looks like an
interstellar Denny's.

1353
00:58:16,333 --> 00:58:17,167
Great.

1354
00:58:18,767 --> 00:58:21,167
- [Joel] Wow, they had
more switches than we do.

1355
00:58:26,300 --> 00:58:27,333
(gasping)

1356
00:58:27,367 --> 00:58:29,467
- [Tom] Did you float an
air biscuit or is that me?

1357
00:58:33,600 --> 00:58:34,667
- Captain Ross?

1358
00:58:34,700 --> 00:58:36,700
- [Crow] Hey, their doggy
left all their bones here.

1359
00:58:36,733 --> 00:58:38,067
- [Joel] That's the people,
you dolt.

1360
00:58:38,100 --> 00:58:39,100
- [Crow] Oh.

1361
00:58:43,033 --> 00:58:44,167
- [Tom] Nice wallet.

1362
00:58:44,200 --> 00:58:46,433
- [Joel] That's his
sternum, don't touch it!

1363
00:58:51,033 --> 00:58:53,200
- I wanna check every
compartment in this ship.

1364
00:58:54,567 --> 00:58:56,767
I'm grabbing the chief here.

1365
00:59:05,633 --> 00:59:09,167
- [Joel] Huh, it says
"Thou shalt not ki--"

1366
00:59:09,200 --> 00:59:11,900
- [Crow] Uh, that was in
the other show.

1367
00:59:11,933 --> 00:59:13,267
- [Tom] It's a Close N' Play

1368
00:59:17,933 --> 00:59:20,167
- [Joel] It says,
"Ahab was obsessed

1369
00:59:20,200 --> 00:59:22,033
"with the Great White One."

1370
00:59:24,900 --> 00:59:26,967
It's a well, there's a
little girl down there!

1371
00:59:27,000 --> 00:59:27,900
- Well, it's the same situation

1372
00:59:27,933 --> 00:59:29,467
down in the maneuvering room.

1373
00:59:29,500 --> 00:59:31,133
The entire engineering crew.

1374
00:59:31,167 --> 00:59:32,033
- [Crow] The maneuvering room?

1375
00:59:32,067 --> 00:59:33,767
Don't you mean the bathroom?

1376
00:59:35,467 --> 00:59:36,933
- Just like it, too.

1377
00:59:36,967 --> 00:59:38,733
- There's one thing that
puzzles me, doc.

1378
00:59:38,767 --> 00:59:39,833
- [Crow] Fractions.

1379
00:59:39,867 --> 00:59:41,867
- One hatch is left
standing open.

1380
00:59:41,900 --> 00:59:44,400
And looks like some of
them have been forced.

1381
00:59:44,433 --> 00:59:46,667
- [Tom] Kinda like your
characterization.

1382
00:59:46,700 --> 00:59:48,667
- Someone else has
searched through the ship?

1383
00:59:48,700 --> 00:59:50,100
- Yeah, something like that.

1384
00:59:57,533 --> 00:59:59,267
- We've accounted for
all but five.

1385
01:00:02,167 --> 01:00:04,167
- There were five survivors.

1386
01:00:04,200 --> 01:00:06,133
- You mean that recorder
still works after 18 years?

1387
01:00:06,167 --> 01:00:07,400
- [Tom] Yep, it's on
eight-track.

1388
01:00:07,433 --> 01:00:09,100
- Emergency power pack,

1389
01:00:09,133 --> 01:00:10,867
it's as good as the day
it was installed.

1390
01:00:10,900 --> 01:00:11,733
Listen to this.

1391
01:00:14,567 --> 01:00:16,300
- [Recording] Now thete
are only three of us.

1392
01:00:16,333 --> 01:00:17,967
I don't expect
Sergeant Long to last

1393
01:00:18,000 --> 01:00:19,700
more than a few days now.

1394
01:00:19,733 --> 01:00:20,933
- [Crow] Long won't last long.

1395
01:00:20,967 --> 01:00:23,733
- [Recording] Has caused
lost of sight in both eyes,

1396
01:00:23,767 --> 01:00:27,067
and his brain seems to
have been damaged somehow.

1397
01:00:27,100 --> 01:00:30,433
I'm also certain that my
fever will soon overcome me.

1398
01:00:30,467 --> 01:00:32,133
There are no more drugs
aboard the ship.

1399
01:00:32,167 --> 01:00:34,267
- [Joel] This planet's
totally dry, dude.

1400
01:00:34,300 --> 01:00:36,800
Don't look to be scorin' nothin'
here.

1401
01:00:36,833 --> 01:00:39,467
- [Recording] Year one,
74th day.

1402
01:00:40,567 --> 01:00:42,367
- That's the last report.

1403
01:00:42,400 --> 01:00:43,300
- 74 long days.

1404
01:00:45,467 --> 01:00:48,700
Watching the sky,
waiting for us.

1405
01:00:50,067 --> 01:00:50,967
Waiting for death.

1406
01:00:52,767 --> 01:00:53,933
- [Crow] Nice speech, Jim.

1407
01:00:53,967 --> 01:00:57,533
- None of us knew it would
take us 18 years to get back.

1408
01:00:57,567 --> 01:00:59,767
The important thing is,
he knew we would.

1409
01:01:00,767 --> 01:01:01,667
- Thank god we did.

1410
01:01:02,833 --> 01:01:05,500
- You think they might be
alive, up in the mountains?

1411
01:01:05,533 --> 01:01:06,800
- It's possible.

1412
01:01:06,833 --> 01:01:08,433
(loud groaning)

1413
01:01:08,467 --> 01:01:09,833
- [Joel] Jim's constipated.

1414
01:01:11,800 --> 01:01:13,633
- Hey chief, what's wrong?

1415
01:01:13,667 --> 01:01:14,733
(screaming)

1416
01:01:14,767 --> 01:01:16,900
- What's wrong with him, doc?

1417
01:01:16,933 --> 01:01:18,300
- I don't know.

1418
01:01:18,333 --> 01:01:19,733
- [Joel] Why don't you ask him?

1419
01:01:22,833 --> 01:01:24,033
- Quick, get back!

1420
01:01:27,333 --> 01:01:28,733
- [Tom] Oh my god, how horrible,

1421
01:01:28,767 --> 01:01:30,900
to be killed by a plush toy!

1422
01:01:32,033 --> 01:01:32,900
- A tarantula.

1423
01:01:32,933 --> 01:01:34,533
Don't make amu quick moves.

1424
01:01:34,567 --> 01:01:37,433
Doc, keep perfectly still.

1425
01:01:37,467 --> 01:01:38,633
Let me have your laser gun.

1426
01:01:38,667 --> 01:01:39,567
- Yes, sir.

1427
01:01:39,600 --> 01:01:41,367
- [Crow] Kinda late now,
isn't it?

1428
01:01:46,700 --> 01:01:48,133
- Careful Scott, he sees you.

1429
01:01:48,167 --> 01:01:49,433
He can spring that far.

1430
01:01:49,467 --> 01:01:50,600
- [Tom] We rigged him that way.

1431
01:01:50,633 --> 01:01:52,200
- Look out, he's gonna jump!

1432
01:01:52,233 --> 01:01:54,567
(exploding)

1433
01:01:57,200 --> 01:02:00,567
- [Tom] The hopping
spider of Rylos !V.

1434
01:02:00,600 --> 01:02:02,900
- [Joel] Oh, I guess
he's really an angel now.

1435
01:02:04,067 --> 01:02:06,800
- I think he died more
from shock than the poison.

1436
01:02:06,833 --> 01:02:08,267
- Little lady seeks death.

1437
01:02:08,300 --> 01:02:09,500
- [Tom] Quick diagnosis.

1438
01:02:10,500 --> 01:02:11,333
- Let's go.

1439
01:02:13,033 --> 01:02:15,100
- [Crow] Well don't
everybody be so sad.

1440
01:02:26,033 --> 01:02:27,200
- What else is on the tape?

1441
01:02:28,233 --> 01:02:29,967
- [Joel] Eddie Money,
Two Tickets to Paradise,

1442
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:31,200
that's about it.

1443
01:02:31,233 --> 01:02:32,067
The DeFranco Family.

1444
01:02:32,100 --> 01:02:34,133
I don't think you'd like it.

1445
01:02:34,167 --> 01:02:35,767
- Two of them did it.

1446
01:02:35,800 --> 01:02:36,767
They murdered Ross.

1447
01:02:38,733 --> 01:02:40,733
- This'll hit the
admiral pretty hard.

1448
01:02:40,767 --> 01:02:41,900
- Yeah.

1449
01:02:41,933 --> 01:02:43,433
Hit them pretty hard too, doc.

1450
01:02:43,467 --> 01:02:44,267
- [Tom] Wrecked 'em?

1451
01:02:44,300 --> 01:02:45,967
Damn near killed 'em!

1452
01:02:46,000 --> 01:02:47,833
- [Crow] And so Johnny Longtorso

1453
01:02:47,867 --> 01:02:50,767
and his industrial band of
bad boy spacefarin' pals

1454
01:02:50,800 --> 01:02:53,433
step out into the cold
air of Central Park.

1455
01:02:54,833 --> 01:02:58,433
(instrumental theme music)

1456
01:03:06,333 --> 01:03:07,167
- Oooh.

1457
01:03:11,133 --> 01:03:12,033
(Joel singing)

1458
01:03:12,067 --> 01:03:13,133
- I love it.

1459
01:03:13,167 --> 01:03:15,100
- [Tom] All that is is my
mother's shower curtain.

1460
01:03:16,167 --> 01:03:17,233
- Oh yes, Tang.

1461
01:03:18,867 --> 01:03:21,133
- [Joel] Crazy woman, I
offer her something to drink,

1462
01:03:21,167 --> 01:03:23,167
she thinks it's my name
all of a sudden.

1463
01:03:24,200 --> 01:03:25,067
- [Tom] What the?

1464
01:03:33,800 --> 01:03:36,367
- How long have your mother
and father been gone, Tang?

1465
01:03:36,400 --> 01:03:37,833
- [Crow] You mean frozen?

1466
01:03:38,667 --> 01:03:40,700
- [Tang] I was a child.

1467
01:03:40,733 --> 01:03:43,167
- Then who taught you
to speak, how to live?

1468
01:03:44,033 --> 01:03:44,867
- Mother teach.

1469
01:03:45,800 --> 01:03:46,833
She live until...

1470
01:03:46,867 --> 01:03:49,067
- [Tom] She held me
back in the third grade.

1471
01:03:51,433 --> 01:03:53,600
- Do you live here all alone?

1472
01:03:53,633 --> 01:03:55,000
- [Tang] Yes.

1473
01:03:55,033 --> 01:03:55,967
Alone.

1474
01:03:56,000 --> 01:03:58,333
- [Crow] If you don't
counf my 27 monkeys.

1475
01:03:58,367 --> 01:03:59,833
- Are there other people
on this planet?

1476
01:03:59,867 --> 01:04:01,167
- Yes, there are others.

1477
01:04:03,200 --> 01:04:05,533
Savages who hate and kill.

1478
01:04:06,900 --> 01:04:08,967
They do not want Tang to
live in their country.

1479
01:04:09,000 --> 01:04:10,333
- [Joel] Oh, you mean
Crash Orange,

1480
01:04:10,367 --> 01:04:12,933
Goofy Grape, Lefty Lemon,
that whole gang?

1481
01:04:12,967 --> 01:04:15,267
